00:51:22,120 --> 00:51:29,980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Vice Chair Sancho Fernando "Ando" Oaminal and Vice Chair Niko Raul Daza, you have the floor.

696
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:59,980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues, ladies and gentlemen, please allow me to welcome to the House of Representatives the Department of Foreign Affairs, headed by Secretary Maria Theresa P. Lazaro, together with its attached agencies: the Foreign Service Institute, the Presidential Commission on Visiting Forces, and the UNESCO National Commission of the Philippines. It is my honor, together with my colleague Representative Niko Raul Daza, to sponsor

697
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:29,980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the DFA's proposed budget for fiscal year 2027 in the amount of approximately 35.17 billion. This represents a 21.77% increase from the fiscal year 2026 GAA and will support the department's work in national security, economic diplomacy, consular services, assistance to Filipinos overseas, and organizational development. Fellow

698
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:59,980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: members of Congress, the Department of Foreign Affairs plays a central role in advancing and protecting Philippine interests abroad. Its work remains anchored on the three pillars of Philippine foreign policy: preservation and enhancement of national security, promotion and attainment of economic security, and protection of the rights and promotion of the welfare and interests of Filipinos overseas. This year the Philippines has taken on a major regional responsibility as chair of ASEAN

699
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:29,980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: under the theme "Navigating Our Future, Together." Through our chairship, the Philippines has helped advance key regional priorities and would have hosted more than 640 meetings throughout the year at the leaders', ministerial, officials' and technical levels. A key outcome of the May 2026 summit in Cebu is the ASEAN Leaders' Declaration on Maritime Cooperation, which provides for

700
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:59,980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the establishment of the ASEAN Maritime Center to be hosted by the Philippines. Beyond ASEAN, the department continues to strengthen the Philippines' bilateral and multilateral partnerships in pursuit of mutually beneficial cooperation. These engagements serve to build and strengthen alliances and partnerships, promote Philippine economic interests, particularly trade and investment, and strengthen people-to-people ties. Maritime security remains a major foreign policy priority.

701
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:29,000
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: This year marked the tenth anniversary of the 2016 arbitral award. The 1982 United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and the 2016 award remain the twin anchors of our foreign policy in the maritime space as we protect and promote our sovereignty, sovereign rights and jurisdiction in the West Philippine Sea. Mr. Speaker, service to our Filipinos overseas remains at the core of the department's work. This

702
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:33,660
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: responsibility has become even more important amid continuing conflict in the Middle East.

703
00:54:33,660 --> 00:54:40,160
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The DFA, through our foreign service posts, continues to assist Filipinos affected by hostilities

704
00:54:40,160 --> 00:54:45,640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and coordinates closely with the Department of Migrant Workers and other partner agencies

705
00:54:45,640 --> 00:54:48,760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: on repatriation and other forms of assistance.

706
00:54:49,780 --> 00:54:55,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The Department continues its diplomatic engagements with governments and international organizations

707
00:54:55,600 --> 00:55:00,580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: to help safeguard Filipino seafarers and Philippine-flagged vessels

708
00:55:00,580 --> 00:55:05,440
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: operating in areas affected by conflict and heightened security risks.

709
00:55:06,160 --> 00:55:11,020
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: These efforts underscore the need for the Department to maintain the capability to respond quickly

710
00:55:11,020 --> 00:55:15,040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: whenever the safety and welfare of Filipinos overseas are at risk.

711
00:55:15,800 --> 00:55:19,540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The DFA likewise continues to work closely with the Department of Migrant Workers

712
00:55:19,540 --> 00:55:21,740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: in serving Filipinos overseas.

713
00:55:22,420 --> 00:55:25,260
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: In countries without a resident migrant workers' office,

714
00:55:25,600 --> 00:55:30,160
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: the DFA continues to play a lead role in looking after our Kababayans.

715
00:55:30,700 --> 00:55:34,320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The Department also remains responsible for overseas Filipinos

716
00:55:34,320 --> 00:55:36,880
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: who are not classified as migrant workers,

717
00:55:37,500 --> 00:55:42,520
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: including students, tourists, permanent residents, and other Filipino nationals.

718
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:47,500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: At the same time, the Department continues to bring consular services closer to the public.

719
00:55:47,500 --> 00:55:52,800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: In 2026, the DFA processed more than 1.5 million passports,

720
00:55:53,480 --> 00:55:55,260
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: issued hundreds of thousands,

721
00:55:55,600 --> 00:56:03,040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and continued to provide services through its 42 consular offices nationwide.

722
00:56:03,600 --> 00:56:09,620
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The 2027 budget will support preparations for the next-generation Philippine passport,

723
00:56:10,120 --> 00:56:13,120
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: which is expected to feature enhanced security features,

724
00:56:13,740 --> 00:56:16,100
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: updated contactless chip technology,

725
00:56:16,520 --> 00:56:19,900
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and an option for additional passport pages.

726
00:56:19,900 --> 00:56:23,920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: It will likewise support continued investments in ICT,

727
00:56:24,940 --> 00:56:25,440
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: cybersecurity,

728
00:56:25,600 --> 00:56:27,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and data protection.

729
00:56:27,600 --> 00:56:31,040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: The DFA is also expanding the reach of the Foreign Service

730
00:56:31,040 --> 00:56:34,360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: through the opening of new posts in strategic locations,

731
00:56:34,360 --> 00:56:39,320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: including our embassies in Accra, Ghana, and Astana, Kazakhstan,

732
00:56:39,320 --> 00:56:41,960
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: which are expected to open this year,

733
00:56:41,960 --> 00:56:45,240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: and our Consulate General in Miami, Florida,

734
00:56:45,240 --> 00:56:47,740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: which is scheduled for 2027.

735
00:56:47,740 --> 00:56:52,320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: These posts will help bring services closer to Filipino communities abroad

736
00:56:52,320 --> 00:56:55,580
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: while strengthening the country's political and economic engagement.

737
00:56:55,600 --> 00:56:58,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues,

738
00:56:59,380 --> 00:57:04,780
