Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct?

772
00:58:41,580 --> 00:58:42,420
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

773
00:58:43,920 --> 00:58:51,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yet, records would show that turnout remains low during recent years.

774
00:58:51,900 --> 00:58:52,500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct?

775
00:58:53,800 --> 00:58:55,200
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: That's correct, Mr. Speaker.

776
00:58:55,900 --> 00:58:57,840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: May I know what's the reason behind?

777
00:58:58,540 --> 00:59:01,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How come the turnout remains so low from previous years?

778
00:59:02,200 --> 00:59:08,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, maraming factors to consider bakit medyo mababa yung turnout.

779
00:59:08,600 --> 00:59:12,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And a few of which are the mobility of overseas Filipinos.

780
00:59:13,200 --> 00:59:13,800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Work relationships.

781
00:59:13,920 --> 00:59:14,860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Related constraints.

782
00:59:15,240 --> 00:59:17,540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Minsan, hindi po pinapayagan ng mga employees nila.

783
00:59:18,160 --> 00:59:21,360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Country-specific restrictions and geographic dispersion.

784
00:59:21,880 --> 00:59:24,660
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Political engagement or lack of confidence.

785
00:59:25,660 --> 00:59:28,880
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And we have a limited awareness of the registration and the process.

786
00:59:29,260 --> 00:59:42,320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yung iba po nating kababayan, hirap po sila to participate kasi hindi po nila alam yung how to go about it and how to participate in the electoral procedure, Mr. Speaker.

787
00:59:42,320 --> 00:59:45,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, this is your sponsor.

788
00:59:45,600 --> 00:59:47,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You mentioned lack of confidence.

789
00:59:48,400 --> 00:59:50,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can you elaborate what does it mean?

790
00:59:53,700 --> 00:59:57,820
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, lack of confidence.

791
00:59:57,820 --> 00:59:58,920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, lack of confidence.

792
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:21,060
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: When I say lack of confidence po, Mr. Speaker, ibig sabihin po, yung mga workers po, they are not that confident yet in the process by which the elections is being done.

793
01:00:21,060 --> 01:00:42,120
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: They need more awareness, Mr. Speaker, kaya po yung Department of Foreign Affairs are consistently undergoing trainings and information campaigns to educate better these intended participants of the electoral process, Mr. Speaker.

794
01:00:42,120 --> 01:00:49,500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So in short, the lack of confidence, when you translate that to Tagalog, it means wala silang tiwala? Ganun ba yun?

795
01:00:50,080 --> 01:00:51,040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Sa proseso?

796
01:00:51,060 --> 01:01:09,280
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, it's not na wala po silang tiwala, Mr. Speaker, pero in a way din po, parang some of them feel that their votes do not necessarily make an impact, kaya hindi na lang po sila bumuboto.

797
01:01:09,280 --> 01:01:21,040
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So they need more awareness and more information campaigns po, Mr. Speaker. Kumbaga, kailangan po ipaintindi po sa kanila na every vote counts.

798
01:01:21,060 --> 01:01:25,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

799
01:01:25,900 --> 01:01:32,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How much funds were allocated in the previous years for overseas absentee voting?

800
01:01:33,000 --> 01:01:49,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And in connection to that, could you explain the reasons for this low voter turnout and if this is isolated only in specific jurisdictions or is this prevalent in all countries where we have overseas voters?

801
01:01:51,060 --> 01:02:00,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, we are just gathering the data in terms of yung amount expended in the previous years.

802
01:02:01,200 --> 01:02:08,920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But for the turnout, it seems to be consistent in the different regions of the world.

803
01:02:09,820 --> 01:02:20,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Sa highest po is only 24.16%, which is in the Asia and the Pacific, and the lowest is in North and Latin Americas, which is 7.9%.

804
01:02:21,060 --> 01:02:28,680
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And as I've mentioned earlier, Mr. Speaker, maraming factors po ang nag-contribute due to the low turnout.

805
01:02:28,920 --> 01:02:39,320
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But the department is already doubling its efforts, ensuring that in the next electoral process, this will greatly improve, Mr. Speaker.

806
01:02:40,440 --> 01:02:47,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Have you tried the COMLEC na magkaroon kayo ng consultation or technical working group when it comes to this?

807
01:02:47,860 --> 01:02:50,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: At least, are they involved, COMLEC?

808
01:02:50,060 --> 01:02:50,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: COMLEC?

809
01:02:51,060 --> 01:02:56,840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, definitely, Mr. Speaker. The COMLEC is very much involved in this procedure.

810
01:02:58,840 --> 01:03:08,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My follow-up question, just to put this in context, how many overseas registered voters do we have in 2025, if we have the figures on hand?

811
01:03:08,760 --> 01:03:19,800
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: As of 2025, Mr. Speaker, there are 1,241,690 registered overseas voters, to be exact po.

812
01:03:20,600 --> 01:03:21,000
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Out of?

813
01:03:21,060 --> 01:03:26,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Out of this 1.2 million voters, how many had actually voted?

814
01:03:27,580 --> 01:03:37,500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Out of the 1.2 million po, Mr. Speaker, 228,000 approximately were able to actually vote, which is equivalent to 18.4%, Mr. Speaker.

815
01:03:37,860 --> 01:03:40,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, napakababa pala ng turnout natin.

816
01:03:41,460 --> 01:03:42,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

817
01:03:42,640 --> 01:03:45,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Almost 18%, Mr. Speaker.

818
01:03:45,180 --> 01:03:49,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, ano sa tingin mo ang reason neto?

819
01:03:49,740 --> 01:03:50,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Because you mentioned ago...

820
01:03:51,060 --> 01:03:55,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Lack of confidence, kailangan you have a massive information campaign.

821
01:03:57,040 --> 01:04:05,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Internet voting removed the physical distance problem, but turnout was still only about 18% among OBCS voters.

822
01:04:05,220 --> 01:04:09,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, what does DFA's post-election assessment say?

823
01:04:09,880 --> 01:04:20,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Were the actual barriers pre-voting enrollment, digital literacy, authentication, awareness, trust, connectivity, or something else?

824
01:04:20,320 --> 01:04:21,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or maybe?

825
01:04:21,060 --> 01:04:25,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yung mga kababayan ba natin, natatakot sila because they're not documented?

826
01:04:27,780 --> 01:04:36,840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Several factors mentioned by the good gentleman, Mr. Speaker, contributed po dun sa low turnout.

827
01:04:37,420 --> 01:04:42,080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And yung digital literacy is very important din po.

828
01:04:42,080 --> 01:04:50,080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Isa yun sa malaking reason bakit po hindi nakaboto.

829
01:04:50,080 --> 01:04:53,640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Nakaboto yung iba nating kababayan kahit na gusto po nilang bumoto.

830
01:04:53,640 --> 01:05:10,120
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And that is why in the past several months and in the upcoming months, nagkaroon at magkakaroon po yung DFA ng overseas regional training for continuing overseas voter registration.

831
01:05:10,620 --> 01:05:17,640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Kasama na din po dyan yung process by which on how to exercise their vote, Mr. Speaker.

832
01:05:17,640 --> 01:05:21,420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor,

833
01:05:21,420 --> 01:05:33,260
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I understand that statutory division of responsibility, but DFA operates the foreign service post and undertook information registration activities.

834
01:05:34,160 --> 01:05:40,300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I therefore want DFA's own expenditures and outputs separated from COMELEC.

835
01:05:40,300 --> 01:05:46,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Besides, Mr. Speaker, overseas registration for the succeeding election cycle,

836
01:05:47,640 --> 01:05:57,440
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: already began on December 1, 2025, and is scheduled to continue through September 30, 2027 at embassies and consulates.

837
01:05:58,060 --> 01:06:02,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So I presume we'll be funding these activities again. Am I right?

838
01:06:04,400 --> 01:06:11,560
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker. Nakahiwalay po talaga yung budget ng overseas voting under the DFA.

839
01:06:11,560 --> 01:06:16,560
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: For 2026, nagkaroon po ng 44.4 million separately.

840
01:06:17,640 --> 01:06:19,640
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: For that purpose.

841
01:06:19,860 --> 01:06:27,600
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And iba din po yung budget allocated by the COMELEC, which I do not have any record for.

842
01:06:27,700 --> 01:06:28,920
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: This office does not have any record.

843
01:06:29,020 --> 01:06:33,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So yung sa COMELEC, so you have separate budget with COMELEC. Am I right?

844
01:06:33,420 --> 01:06:34,280
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

845
01:06:34,320 --> 01:06:36,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So paano nyo nire-reconcile yun?

846
01:06:36,740 --> 01:06:38,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Wala bang duplicity?

847
01:06:38,600 --> 01:06:41,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mga mamiya, nag-fund kayo, ganun din sila.

848
01:06:41,000 --> 01:06:47,620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So there will be a separate, may kanya-kanya, baka yung jurisdiction, or how to go.

849
01:06:47,700 --> 01:06:48,080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: About it?

850
01:06:48,880 --> 01:06:56,520
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, as to the details of the budget, kasi part of which is the traveling expenses.

851
01:06:57,300 --> 01:07:02,480
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So yung mga officials po ng COMELEC, dun po nila sinacharge sa office nila sa DFA naman po.

852
01:07:02,580 --> 01:07:05,740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Dito naman po under the DFA training expenses din po.

853
01:07:07,140 --> 01:07:11,360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Training of, there's a counterpart of DFA and there's a counterpart of COMELEC.

854
01:07:11,360 --> 01:07:17,360
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So we assure the good gentleman that there is no duplicity.

855
01:07:17,640 --> 01:07:20,460
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Of the expenses, Mr. Chair.

856
01:07:21,360 --> 01:07:22,500
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Thank you, Mr. Sponsor.

857
01:07:23,320 --> 01:07:28,220
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, before we fund further preparatory activity in 2027,

858
01:07:29,160 --> 01:07:36,740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: when will Congress receive the costed proposal for the hybrid or revised overseas voting system,

859
01:07:37,240 --> 01:07:40,360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: including lessons learned from 2025?

860
01:07:40,360 --> 01:07:51,620
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: I'm sorry, may we repeat the question, Mr. Speaker?

861
01:07:51,620 --> 01:08:02,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, before we fund further preparatory activity for 2027, right now, because asking for another fund for 2027 here in Congress,

862
01:08:03,580 --> 01:08:09,360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: kailan namin matatanggap yung costed proposal for the hybrid or revised overseas voting system,

863
01:08:09,880 --> 01:08:10,340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: including lessons learned from 2025?

864
01:08:10,340 --> 01:08:12,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kailan namin matatanggap yung lessons learned from 2025?

865
01:08:12,780 --> 01:08:16,940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Remember 2025, the turnout was only around 18%.

866
01:08:16,940 --> 01:08:19,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 18% lang, Mr. Chair.

867
01:08:20,060 --> 01:08:22,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The actual votes, right?

868
01:08:22,500 --> 01:08:30,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So ngayon, 2027, yung costing nyo for the preparation for the hybrid or revised overseas voting system.

869
01:08:31,240 --> 01:08:37,600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So anong gagawin natin na hindi natin maulit yung turnout natin na 18%?

870
01:08:38,460 --> 01:08:39,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Chair, part of...

871
01:08:39,860 --> 01:08:49,980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Part po ng activities that the DFA will conduct is yung training and information dissemination po.

872
01:08:49,980 --> 01:08:55,860
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So yung pagpapaintindi po sa ating mga kababayan, how important their vote is.

873
01:08:56,580 --> 01:09:08,480
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So yun po yung nagdodouble efforts yung DFA and of course in partnership with COMELEC to educate our mga kababayan overseas po.

874
01:09:08,820 --> 01:09:08,980
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So that...

875
01:09:09,860 --> 01:09:15,720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yun po yung way na ma-increase po yung turnout natin, Mr. Chair.

876
01:09:15,720 --> 01:09:25,080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And of course, better accessibility to the information needed through postings not only sa consular offices,

877
01:09:25,260 --> 01:09:36,240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: I mean sa foreign posts offices, but also through the direct communication with our recorded kababayans, Mr. Speaker.

878
01:09:37,000 --> 01:09:39,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As you know, Mr. Speaker, 2288 is around...

879
01:09:39,860 --> 01:09:49,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So do you think the 18% will translate maybe half, maybe 50% kaya ba natin by 2028?

880
01:09:49,880 --> 01:10:05,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Otherwise, Mr. Speaker, sayang lang yung pondong ibinibigay natin because we're funding our massive information campaign for our kababayan overseas to make sure na makaboto sila because every vote counts.

881
01:10:05,540 --> 01:10:08,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So do you see in the 20...

882
01:10:09,860 --> 01:10:16,680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or maybe the presidential election, tataas ang ating turnout vote?

883
01:10:17,840 --> 01:10:24,240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: That is the hope and the direction, Mr. Speaker, na mapapataas po yung rate.

884
01:10:24,460 --> 01:10:36,720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And of course, we also are expecting that the COMELEC will double its efforts in increasing the turnout rate, Mr. Speaker.

885
01:10:36,720 --> 01:10:39,720
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: But as far as the DFA is concerned...

886
01:10:39,860 --> 01:10:47,840
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: In coordinating with the overseas Filipino voters, so they're doubling their efforts already po, Mr. Speaker.

887
01:10:47,840 --> 01:10:50,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you for that, good sponsor.

888
01:10:50,880 --> 01:10:55,340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, may I go to one of the crucial mandates of the department?

889
01:10:56,280 --> 01:11:08,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor, can you confirm the report that DFA had already lodged 39 diplomatic protests against China in 2026?

890
01:11:08,120 --> 01:11:14,050
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And 296 from 2022 through 2026?

891
01:11:14,620 --> 01:11:16,380
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, that is correct, Mr. Speaker.

892
01:11:17,840 --> 01:11:28,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The diplomacy program itself is seeking approximately 14.48 billion in 2027. Is this correct?

893
01:11:29,820 --> 01:11:31,340
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Speaker, that's correct.

894
01:11:31,340 --> 01:11:39,340
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: For the next fiscal year, or maybe for the past years, what performance framework does DFA use to determine...

895
01:11:39,860 --> 01:11:45,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ...whether these protests are producing the intended diplomatic outcome?

896
01:11:46,980 --> 01:12:01,140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Speaker, we believe that these diplomatic protests, since these are legal documents, have in a way toned down the aggression of other countries against the Philippines, Mr. Speaker.

897
01:12:02,740 --> 01:12:09,140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Makikita naman po natin na yung DFA, it is their role...

898
01:12:09,860 --> 01:12:21,380
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: ...is to diplomatically negotiate and communicate with other countries, Mr. Chair.

899
01:12:21,800 --> 01:12:39,240
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So, as we see na ngayon, while tensions are still there, pero medyo in a controlled level na po, then that is already an achievement on the part of the DFA, Mr. Chair, na yung mga inisyo na diplomatic notes are effective.

900
01:12:39,240 --> 01:12:39,740
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And in fact...

901
01:12:39,860 --> 01:12:44,900
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And in fact, many of which have been answered by China, Mr. Chair.

902
01:12:45,180 --> 01:12:51,540
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yung iba, maramihan po nila sinagot. Yung iba po, isa-isa nila sinagot.

903
01:12:53,140 --> 01:12:55,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

904
01:12:55,800 --> 01:13:09,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is DFA tracking, for example, whether a protest receives a formal response, whether the complaint of conduct ceases or recurs, whether partner governments...

905
01:13:09,860 --> 01:13:21,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ...issues, supporting statements, whether operational behavior at sea changes, otherwise our protest will just be a mere formality with no outcome?

906
01:13:23,940 --> 01:13:30,700
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: As mentioned, Mr. Chair, there is no one-on-one, one-to-one correspondence on our protests with China.

907
01:13:32,540 --> 01:13:38,700
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yung reply nila, minsan, there are three or four diplomatic notes and they will only reply with one...

908
01:13:39,860 --> 01:13:43,300
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: They will reply to that once, yung three or four diplomatic notes.

909
01:13:43,880 --> 01:13:57,140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: And we can see now, Mr. Chair, humuhupuan naman po yung tensyon as far as yung mga naririnig natin sa news before na there's attack against our fishermen, against our Coast Guard.

910
01:13:57,140 --> 01:14:09,140
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: So ngayon, we are seeing na medyo nagto-tone down po, Mr. Chair, and we believe that this is greatly due also to the diplomatic notes issue.

911
01:14:09,860 --> 01:14:12,460
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: by the Department of Foreign Affairs, Mr. Chair.

912
01:14:12,840 --> 01:14:15,240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

913
01:14:15,920 --> 01:14:34,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: This becomes more relevant because on September 11, following a Philippine Coast Guard report that Chinese forces fired flares toward a Philippine aircraft near Zamora, Subi, and Panganiban Mischief Reefs.

914
01:14:34,320 --> 01:14:38,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The FBI public called on China to cease its activities.

915
01:14:39,860 --> 01:14:47,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: at the futures and reiterated its position under UNCLOS and the 2016 Arbitral Award.

916
01:14:48,720 --> 01:14:49,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct?

917
01:14:50,500 --> 01:14:51,760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Yes, Mr. Chair, that's correct.

918
01:14:53,020 --> 01:14:58,680
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So with respect to the September flare incident, did DFA lodge a diplomatic protest?

919
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:12,080
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Mr. Chair, the DFA is about to send a diplomatic protest on that particular attack, Mr. Chair.

920
01:15:12,440 --> 01:15:15,140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, it happened last week, September 11.

921
01:15:15,320 --> 01:15:15,920
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yes, Mr. Chair.

922
01:15:15,920 --> 01:15:21,420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, isn't it after the incident, the following day, we should launch a protest?

923
01:15:21,540 --> 01:15:24,360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Hindi ba ganun ang SOP natin dyan?

924
01:15:24,700 --> 01:15:26,280
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Not immediately, Mr. Speaker.

925
01:15:26,280 --> 01:15:38,760
Rep. Sancho Fernando "Ando" F. Oaminal: Because the DFA awaits the detailed incident report about the attacks before they send out a diplomatic protest, Mr. Speaker.

926
01:15:39,920 --> 01:15:41,400
