Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang dahilan po,

4321
04:22:36,640 --> 04:22:37,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: normally,

4322
04:22:38,200 --> 04:22:39,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung Filsa,

4323
04:22:39,700 --> 04:22:40,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: as with

4324
04:22:40,200 --> 04:22:41,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: some other agencies,

4325
04:22:42,080 --> 04:22:42,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: normally,

4326
04:22:42,440 --> 04:22:43,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: di na nag-interpelate,

4327
04:22:43,460 --> 04:22:43,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pero,

4328
04:22:44,820 --> 04:22:45,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ina-approve na lang

4329
04:22:45,620 --> 04:22:46,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng Kongreso ang budget.

4330
04:22:46,980 --> 04:22:47,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This time around though,

4331
04:22:48,860 --> 04:22:49,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na obliga tayo

4332
04:22:49,960 --> 04:22:50,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dahil

4333
04:22:50,600 --> 04:22:51,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: no less

4334
04:22:51,120 --> 04:22:51,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: than the President

4335
04:22:51,880 --> 04:22:53,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: mentioned

4336
04:22:53,240 --> 04:22:54,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the Philippines Space Agency

4337
04:22:54,740 --> 04:22:55,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: in his SONA.

4338
04:22:56,320 --> 04:22:56,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba?

4339
04:22:56,620 --> 04:22:57,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Isa sa mga

4340
04:22:57,200 --> 04:22:58,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: highlights

4341
04:22:58,220 --> 04:22:58,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nung SONA

4342
04:22:58,900 --> 04:22:59,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay,

4343
04:22:59,140 --> 04:23:14,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sinabi niya, by 2027, the Philippines will launch its first ever sounding rocket in Cagayan in 2027.

4344
04:23:16,040 --> 04:23:18,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun po ang gusto nating alamin.

4345
04:23:19,280 --> 04:23:22,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At dun ba gagamitin yung budget na ito?

4346
04:23:22,380 --> 04:23:31,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Particularly the P739.9 million for research and development, policy development, and capacity building.

4347
04:23:31,840 --> 04:23:37,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Could you tell us more about this program of VILSA, yung rocket?

4348
04:23:39,660 --> 04:23:45,700
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, Mr. Speaker. Only a very small portion of that will be used for the launch of the sounding rocket.

4349
04:23:45,700 --> 04:23:51,860
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: But to give you an update on the pronouncement of the President last sauna,

4350
04:23:51,860 --> 04:23:59,480
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: last August 4, official project kick-off with the VILSA, DICT, CESA, Ascend International Gateway,

4351
04:23:59,840 --> 04:24:02,760
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Perigee Aerospace Incorporated, and Perigee Manila,

4352
04:24:03,160 --> 04:24:10,800
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: affirming its commitment towards implementing the test launch of the sounding rocket within the first quarter of 2027.

4353
04:24:11,100 --> 04:24:19,700
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: And last August 11, VILSA engineers left for Korea to undertake 10 weeks of technical and hands-on training on building the sounding rocket.

4354
04:24:19,700 --> 04:24:21,700
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: And up to this date, the flight...

4355
04:24:21,860 --> 04:24:25,660
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The flight model of the rocket is being assembled with tests to be undertaken.

4356
04:24:26,180 --> 04:24:32,960
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The rocket is set to be completed and shipped to the Philippines in October on track for the scheduled launch next year, Mr. Speaker.

4357
04:24:33,760 --> 04:24:42,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, so nabanggit niyo po, VILSA involved with other agencies, including a private company called Perigee.

4358
04:24:43,460 --> 04:24:45,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Korean firm po ba ito?

4359
04:24:45,980 --> 04:24:48,240
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, it is a Korean firm, Mr. Speaker.

4360
04:24:48,240 --> 04:24:51,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ito yung kapartner ng VILSA.

4361
04:24:51,860 --> 04:24:55,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa pag-develop at pag-manufacture ng rocket, tama po ba?

4362
04:24:56,120 --> 04:24:57,040
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Tama, Mr. Speaker.

4363
04:24:57,300 --> 04:25:04,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. At tinatawag yung rocket, tinatawag na sounding rocket.

4364
04:25:05,120 --> 04:25:08,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So pwede po bang mapaliwanag, ano yung sabihin ng sounding rocket?

4365
04:25:16,440 --> 04:25:21,840
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: It will be a test launch, Mr. Speaker, but a sounding rocket can be used to

4366
04:25:21,860 --> 04:25:27,840
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: study weather and atmosphere conditions, radiation, space physics, communications, and new technologies.

4367
04:25:27,840 --> 04:25:38,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, so ang intindi ko po, yung sounding rocket, parang siyang mas maliit na rocket, mainly for research purposes, and sounding rockets are suborbital.

4368
04:25:38,200 --> 04:25:48,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, hindi po pa aabot sa outer space technically, but its main use will be for research, scientific purposes.

4369
04:25:48,620 --> 04:25:51,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, so nasa ganung level po.

4370
04:25:51,860 --> 04:26:05,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So our concern po natin ay, okay, meron bang aspeto ng technology transfer at sinasabi, pag-develop ng industriya,

4371
04:26:05,980 --> 04:26:17,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang ayaw po natin mangyari, ito na naman, tag-assemble lang tayo, pero in the end, pag umalis yung kumpanya, in this case, Perigee, wala na naman tayong sariling industriya.

4372
04:26:17,280 --> 04:26:21,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ba ang perspektiba ng VILSA?

4373
04:26:21,860 --> 04:26:46,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: As far as, at least as far as the Acting Director General is concerned, I had the opportunity to speak with her before this interpellation, Mr. Speaker, si Acting Director General Gay Jane P. Perez, physics professor po yan sa UP, at genuine rocket scientist.

4374
04:26:46,860 --> 04:26:50,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano po ba ang perspective ng VILSA?

4375
04:26:51,860 --> 04:26:55,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dito sa space industry, kumbaga.

4376
04:26:56,980 --> 04:27:02,720
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, meron tayong technology transfer. In fact, meron na mga trainings ongoing ngayon.

4377
04:27:03,380 --> 04:27:12,080
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: But the test launch shall be the next step in building capabilities that directly affect the country's economy, resilience, and long-term national interest.

4378
04:27:12,080 --> 04:27:20,700
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yung objective is not simply to launch a rocket, it is to build the people, technology, regulatory framework, safety procedure, and infrastructure

4379
04:27:20,700 --> 04:27:21,700
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: that will allow the people to be able to fly.

4380
04:27:21,700 --> 04:27:21,820
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: that will allow the people to be able to fly.

4381
04:27:21,820 --> 04:27:21,840
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: that will allow the people to be able to fly.

4382
04:27:21,860 --> 04:27:24,640
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: That will allow the Philippines to develop its own launch capability.

4383
04:27:25,480 --> 04:27:29,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, allow the Philippines to develop its own launch capability.

4384
04:27:30,580 --> 04:27:33,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: We will pursue that a little bit, in a little bit.

4385
04:27:33,900 --> 04:27:38,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nabanggit nyo yung maliit na bahagi lang yung para sa launch.

4386
04:27:38,580 --> 04:27:40,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magkano po yung gagastusin for the launch?

4387
04:27:46,300 --> 04:27:48,720
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: This year, Mr. Speaker, it will be a hundred million.

4388
04:27:49,140 --> 04:27:51,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hundred million of the 739 million.

4389
04:27:51,860 --> 04:27:52,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4390
04:27:53,260 --> 04:27:55,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For this year. How about for next year?

4391
04:27:56,380 --> 04:27:59,620
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: For next year, it will just be six million. Over six million.

4392
04:27:59,720 --> 04:28:02,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, one hundred million this year, and then six million next year.

4393
04:28:02,860 --> 04:28:09,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, the rest of the budget, nabanggit nyo po, will be for developing and launching another satellite.

4394
04:28:09,280 --> 04:28:13,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Would you tell us more about this satellite? Mula?

4395
04:28:15,940 --> 04:28:20,220
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, it will be used in developing the Mula 2 satellite, Mr. Chair.

4396
04:28:20,860 --> 04:28:21,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para saan po yung Mula?

4397
04:28:21,860 --> 04:28:32,240
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yung Mula 2 satellite natin, isang multi-spectral unit for land assessment, satellite, earth observation satellite,

4398
04:28:32,560 --> 04:28:40,300
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: being developed by FILSA to generate satellite data to benefit applications in agriculture, environmental protection and monitoring,

4399
04:28:40,840 --> 04:28:46,200
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: natural resource management, disaster risk reduction, and national security, among others.

4400
04:28:46,200 --> 04:28:51,200
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mula shall have a 5M multi-spectral imager, allowing the satellite...

4401
04:28:51,860 --> 04:28:59,060
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: to capture up to 139,000 square kilometers of satellite images per day.

4402
04:28:59,520 --> 04:29:06,120
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The development of Mula was started by DOST in 2021, and was continued in 2023 by FILSA.

4403
04:29:06,940 --> 04:29:10,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Thank you for that. So, mainly, imaging satellite, ganun po ba?

4404
04:29:10,900 --> 04:29:14,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At gagamitin para sa, among others, agrikultura?

4405
04:29:14,720 --> 04:29:15,520
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

4406
04:29:15,540 --> 04:29:15,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganun.

4407
04:29:16,300 --> 04:29:18,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, you did also mention national security.

4408
04:29:19,720 --> 04:29:21,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, baka pwede na nating isegway.

4409
04:29:21,500 --> 04:29:21,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit?

4410
04:29:21,860 --> 04:29:23,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po may national security?

4411
04:29:25,480 --> 04:29:29,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Could you just explain? Ano yung role sa national security?

4412
04:29:31,360 --> 04:29:35,420
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: It is included in the Philippine Space Act, Mr. Chair.

4413
04:29:36,020 --> 04:29:43,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. And as I understand, in the Philippine Space Council, ay co-chair po. Tama po ba?

4414
04:29:43,520 --> 04:29:47,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is it DOST and BND Secretary?

4415
04:29:48,880 --> 04:29:50,940
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Co-Vice Chair ang DOST, Mr. Speaker.

4416
04:29:50,940 --> 04:29:51,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, co-Vice Chair.

4417
04:29:51,860 --> 04:29:56,330
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang chair po ay ang...

4418
04:29:56,330 --> 04:29:57,670
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Our president is the

4419
04:29:57,670 --> 04:29:58,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pangulo mismo.

4420
04:29:58,380 --> 04:29:58,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4421
04:29:59,180 --> 04:30:00,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So,

4422
04:30:00,000 --> 04:30:10,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: well, historically po, ang space sector, aerospace industry, including outer space,

4423
04:30:11,600 --> 04:30:15,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: historically, magpipit na magkaugnay naman talaga yung militar at sibilyan.

4424
04:30:16,500 --> 04:30:16,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

4425
04:30:17,600 --> 04:30:20,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At so, I suppose, kaya ganun.

4426
04:30:22,500 --> 04:30:28,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero ngayon, napapanahon, at in fact, sa gera,

4427
04:30:28,080 --> 04:30:35,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang tinuturing na stratehikong lugar, ang kalawakan.

4428
04:30:35,940 --> 04:30:43,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, control of outer space means control of, I mean, you know,

4429
04:30:43,420 --> 04:30:47,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: it's a requisite for control over everything below it.

4430
04:30:47,820 --> 04:30:48,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Parang ganun.

4431
04:30:49,100 --> 04:30:55,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ngayon, ang tanong, dahil may national security aspect dito,

4432
04:30:55,140 --> 04:30:57,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and this involves manufacturing,

4433
04:30:58,080 --> 04:31:01,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and development of certain advanced technologies.

4434
04:31:02,900 --> 04:31:07,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ang pangunahing inisyatiba ng Malacanang,

4435
04:31:07,740 --> 04:31:10,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng Marcos Administration, kaugnay dyan ngayon,

4436
04:31:10,300 --> 04:31:11,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay yung Pax Silica.

4437
04:31:12,760 --> 04:31:18,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, may involvement ba ang FILSA at ang programa nila,

4438
04:31:18,700 --> 04:31:21,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang mga programa nila sa Pax Silica?

4439
04:31:23,300 --> 04:31:24,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil yung Pax Silica,

4440
04:31:25,820 --> 04:31:27,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang pangunahing concern ng USG,

4441
04:31:28,080 --> 04:31:30,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dyan is the Defense Industrial Base of the United States.

4442
04:31:31,660 --> 04:31:35,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And, inevitably, kasama doon, yung rockets, yung satellites,

4443
04:31:36,340 --> 04:31:38,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and missiles.

4444
04:31:39,760 --> 04:31:40,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Iyan ang ginagawa ng FILSA.

4445
04:31:41,100 --> 04:31:43,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, involved po ba ang FILSA sa Pax Silica?

4446
04:31:44,140 --> 04:31:48,240
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, FILSA is not involved or connected with Pax Silica.

4447
04:31:48,920 --> 04:31:50,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Not involved.

4448
04:31:51,300 --> 04:31:53,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Will it ever be involved?

4449
04:31:53,800 --> 04:31:53,920
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: No.

4450
04:31:58,080 --> 04:32:00,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Or, will it never be involved?

4451
04:32:02,340 --> 04:32:05,660
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The agency has no knowledge about it, Mr. Chair.

4452
04:32:05,740 --> 04:32:07,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No knowledge about it.

4453
04:32:07,560 --> 04:32:10,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, may lupa kayo sa New Clark City.

4454
04:32:12,060 --> 04:32:12,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

4455
04:32:13,340 --> 04:32:17,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And, in fact, yung lupa nyo ay gagamitin para sa Pax Silica.

4456
04:32:17,460 --> 04:32:18,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba?

4457
04:32:20,120 --> 04:32:21,200
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, Mr. Chair.

4458
04:32:21,300 --> 04:32:21,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O, tama.

4459
04:32:21,800 --> 04:32:23,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, may involvement.

4460
04:32:24,060 --> 04:32:27,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kahit sa ganong level, ano po mangyayari sa inyong lupa?

4461
04:32:28,080 --> 04:32:31,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And, yet, you say you're not involved.

4462
04:32:31,480 --> 04:32:31,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano yun?

4463
04:32:32,280 --> 04:32:33,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Please clarify.

4464
04:32:33,700 --> 04:32:35,980
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The agency will relocate, Mr. Chair.

4465
04:32:36,440 --> 04:32:38,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The agency will relocate.

4466
04:32:38,260 --> 04:32:43,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, gagamitin ang lupa nyo para sa Pax Silica sa New Clark City,

4467
04:32:44,080 --> 04:32:47,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pero magre-relocate kayo.

4468
04:32:48,140 --> 04:32:48,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4469
04:32:49,660 --> 04:32:50,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po?

4470
04:32:51,040 --> 04:32:51,780
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, Mr. Chair.

4471
04:32:51,780 --> 04:32:57,900
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: BCDA will relocate the land, Mr. Chair.

4472
04:32:58,080 --> 04:32:59,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, okay.

4473
04:33:00,280 --> 04:33:06,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now, you also mentioned CESA earlier as involved in the rocket launch.

4474
04:33:07,000 --> 04:33:09,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At sa kagayan magaganap yung launch.

4475
04:33:09,460 --> 04:33:16,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In fact, saan po ang target ng first test launch ng sounding rocket

4476
04:33:16,100 --> 04:33:20,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: in the first quarter of 2027?

4477
04:33:20,040 --> 04:33:25,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung pinagmalaki ng Pangulo, saan mangyayari yung launch test?

4478
04:33:25,520 --> 04:33:27,160
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: It will be in Cagayan, Mr. Chair.

4479
04:33:27,320 --> 04:33:27,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Where?

4480
04:33:27,760 --> 04:33:28,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In Cagayan?

4481
04:33:28,080 --> 04:33:30,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Cagayan, specifically, Mr. Speaker.

4482
04:33:32,120 --> 04:33:33,400
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: In Lalo Airport.

4483
04:33:33,560 --> 04:33:34,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lalo Airport.

4484
04:33:35,120 --> 04:33:35,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4485
04:33:35,600 --> 04:33:40,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lalo Airport, which also happens to be an EDCA site.

4486
04:33:41,240 --> 04:33:41,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba?

4487
04:33:42,940 --> 04:33:43,920
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, Mr. Chair.

4488
04:33:43,980 --> 04:33:45,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes, it's an EDCA site.

4489
04:33:45,220 --> 04:33:51,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of all places in the Philippines, bakit po sa EDCA site gaganapin yung test launch?

4490
04:33:52,800 --> 04:33:57,760
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Chair, because of the location, aside from the geographic advantages of being in

4491
04:33:57,760 --> 04:34:06,200
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: the country's eastern seaboard, Cagayan has existing infrastructure in place to execute the test launch of a sounding rocket.

4492
04:34:06,820 --> 04:34:15,140
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Furthermore, the area has an institutional and economic zone framework administered by the Cagayan Economic Zone Authority.

4493
04:34:15,140 --> 04:34:16,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4494
04:34:17,720 --> 04:34:25,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, dahil EDCA site po yan, obviously, nandyan po ang presensya ng U.S. military.

4495
04:34:25,480 --> 04:34:26,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It is actively being used.

4496
04:34:27,760 --> 04:34:30,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: By the U.S. military on a rotational basis.

4497
04:34:31,040 --> 04:34:38,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang alam po natin, yung mga helicopters ng U.S., yan ang ginagamit ng lunsaran.

4498
04:34:38,800 --> 04:34:52,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At nagpapatrolya sila hanggang sa Batanes, sa Nueva Ecija, and parts of the South China Sea, using Lalo as their operating base.

4499
04:34:52,800 --> 04:34:55,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, magkakaroon kayo ng launch doon.

4500
04:34:55,820 --> 04:34:57,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May involvement po ba?

4501
04:34:57,020 --> 04:35:00,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang U.S. military sa proyektong ito?

4502
04:35:01,540 --> 04:35:03,200
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Walang involvement, Mr. Chair.

4503
04:35:03,360 --> 04:35:06,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Wala pong anumang involvement, yun po ang sinasabi natin.

4504
04:35:06,940 --> 04:35:07,240
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes.

4505
04:35:07,400 --> 04:35:08,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa ngayon, wala pong involvement?

4506
04:35:09,560 --> 04:35:10,540
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Sabi po sa agency.

4507
04:35:11,100 --> 04:35:11,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4508
04:35:13,080 --> 04:35:14,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat po.

4509
04:35:14,280 --> 04:35:24,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At least, nagkaroon tayo ng pagkakataon to publicly discuss ano ba talaga yung plano ng Philippine Space Agency.

4510
04:35:24,400 --> 04:35:26,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ba itong binanggit ng Pangulo sa SONA?

4511
04:35:27,020 --> 04:35:36,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At nakikita po natin na, if not now, ay kasama rin po sa proyekto yung mga issue ng national security.

4512
04:35:36,940 --> 04:35:51,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At nakikita na rin po natin, kahit pa pano, ay nadidikit sa usapin ng Paxilica at saka ng U.S. military presence ang proyektong ito.

4513
04:35:51,720 --> 04:35:55,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya babantayan po natin ang further developments dito.

4514
04:35:55,380 --> 04:35:56,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At the same time, of course,

4515
04:35:57,020 --> 04:36:02,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: mahalaga ng mag-develop ng sariling industriya ang mga Pilipino.

4516
04:36:02,860 --> 04:36:06,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kailangan tiyakin natin na ito ay maglilingkod sa interest ng mga Pilipino.

4517
04:36:07,700 --> 04:36:08,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat po.

4518
04:36:09,300 --> 04:36:13,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And I look forward to further discussions with Philza on this matter.

4519
04:36:14,420 --> 04:36:15,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker.

4520
04:36:15,980 --> 04:36:16,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you to the sponsor.

4521
04:36:17,420 --> 04:36:19,740
