4528
04:36:47,860 --> 04:36:50,560
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Asunod ng mga katanungan ng ating congressman Tino.

4529
04:36:51,100 --> 04:36:53,400
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Regarding ho sa rocket launch sa Pilipinas,

4530
04:36:53,780 --> 04:36:56,100
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: ano naman po ang nakikita ng Pilza?

4531
04:36:56,100 --> 04:37:02,380
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Na pangunahing benepisyo at potential risk ng pagkakaroon ng rocket launch capability sa ating bansa.

4532
04:37:03,340 --> 04:37:10,140
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Lalo't sa isang banda ay maaari itong mag-develop ng Pilipino expertise, research, aerospace jobs,

4533
04:37:10,340 --> 04:37:12,780
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: at future commercial space activities.

4534
04:37:13,700 --> 04:37:17,040
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Pero sa kabilang banda, ano naman po ang mga concerns, safety,

4535
04:37:17,800 --> 04:37:21,480
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: concerns sa safety, environmental impact, air and maritime traffic,

4536
04:37:21,980 --> 04:37:24,520
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: at possible rocket debris na kailangang pagandaan?

4537
04:37:26,100 --> 04:37:30,180
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, the test launch is another step towards building capabilities

4538
04:37:30,180 --> 04:37:35,180
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: that directly affect the country's economy, resilience, and long-term national interest

4539
04:37:35,180 --> 04:37:38,320
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: as a space-faring and space-capable nation.

4540
04:37:38,920 --> 04:37:42,080
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The objective is not only to simply just launch a rocket,

4541
04:37:42,080 --> 04:37:48,140
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: it is to build the people, technology, regulatory framework, safety procedures, and infrastructure

4542
04:37:48,140 --> 04:37:52,380
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: that will allow the Philippines to develop its own space launch capability.

4543
04:37:56,100 --> 04:37:59,440
