4669
04:45:24,840 --> 04:45:29,980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The interpolation on the proposed budget of the Philippine Space Agency is hereby.

4670
04:45:30,000 --> 04:45:30,780
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Terminated.

4671
04:45:33,160 --> 04:45:34,480
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

4672
04:45:35,960 --> 04:45:37,960
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Mr. Speaker, move to suspend.

4673
04:45:39,260 --> 04:45:40,120
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Session suspended.

4674
04:48:30,000 --> 04:48:31,040
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Session resumed.

4675
04:48:33,700 --> 04:48:41,420
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I now move to consider the proposed budget of the Climate Change Commission. So moved.

4676
04:48:42,280 --> 04:48:42,980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: In objection?

4677
04:48:43,800 --> 04:48:44,380
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Hearing none.

4678
04:48:44,700 --> 04:48:45,320
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Motion carried.

4679
04:48:46,600 --> 04:48:47,560
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

4680
04:48:49,720 --> 04:48:57,180
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials from the Climate Change Commission,

4681
04:48:57,180 --> 04:49:16,040
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: namely Vice Chairperson and Executive Director Robert E.A. Borje, Commissioner Albert P. De La Cruz, Commissioner Rachel Ann S. Herrera, Deputy Executive Director Romel Antonio Cuenca.

4682
04:49:16,560 --> 04:49:26,800
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: We acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials from the Climate Change Commission, Vice Chairperson and Executive Director Robert Borje,

4683
04:49:27,180 --> 04:49:33,840
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Commissioner Albert P. De La Cruz, Commissioner Rachel Ann S. Herrera, and Deputy Executive Director Romel Antonio Cuenca.

4684
04:49:34,060 --> 04:49:40,280
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Sir, on behalf of Speaker Bojie Dy and Majority Leader Sandro Marcos, welcome to the House of Representatives.

4685
04:49:41,040 --> 04:49:41,640
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

4686
04:49:44,160 --> 04:49:53,840
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative John Geesnell “Baba” Yap, Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations,

4687
04:49:53,920 --> 04:49:57,160
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: to answer the questions on the proposed budget of the Climate Change Commission.

4688
04:49:57,240 --> 04:49:58,560
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: The Climate Change Commission.

4689
04:49:59,100 --> 04:49:59,480
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: So moved.

4690
04:50:00,680 --> 04:50:07,100
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The First District Representative from Bohol, Vice Chair John Geesnell “Baba” Yap.

4691
04:50:07,380 --> 04:50:11,240
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Sir, you may now answer questions and answers from the members.

4692
04:50:12,520 --> 04:50:13,240
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

4693
04:50:14,560 --> 04:50:14,900
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: I'm sorry.

4694
04:50:16,280 --> 04:50:22,100
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues, CCC family, led by Secretary Robert Borje,

4695
04:50:22,100 --> 04:50:23,920
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mayong hapon sa tanan.

4696
04:50:23,920 --> 04:50:32,380
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: It is my privilege to sponsor the proposed Fiscal Year 2027 budget of the Climate Change Commission, or CCC.

4697
04:50:33,040 --> 04:50:42,000
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The government's lead policy-making body tasked to coordinate, monitor, and evaluate our programs and action plans on climate change

4698
04:50:42,000 --> 04:50:50,600
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: and ensure the mainstreaming of climate change into national, sectoral, and local development plans and programs and investment programming.

4699
04:50:51,040 --> 04:50:53,800
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Climate change is no longer a distant threat.

4700
04:50:53,920 --> 04:51:05,920
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Intensifying tropical cyclones, sea-level rise, heavy rainfall events, and increasing temperatures already affect the lives and livelihoods of millions of Filipinos.

4701
04:51:05,920 --> 04:51:19,300
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: From damage to agriculture and infrastructure to escalating economic costs, the burden of climate change continues to grow, falling most heavily on vulnerable communities and sectors.

4702
04:51:20,080 --> 04:51:23,900
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: This reality underscores the need for sustained and sustainable development.

4703
04:51:23,900 --> 04:51:44,800
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The Commission's role is not only to develop climate policies, but to ensure that these are translated into risk-informed planning, investments, and programs that respond to the needs of communities and sectors.

4704
04:51:45,320 --> 04:51:53,800
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The CCC also plays an important role in advancing the country's climate finance agenda and in strengthening the use of

4705
04:51:53,900 --> 04:51:57,240
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: climate risk information to support evidence-based decision-making.

4706
04:51:57,740 --> 04:52:06,160
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: For fiscal year 2027, the proposed budget of the Commission amounts to Php 183,482,000.

4707
04:52:06,820 --> 04:52:17,300
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: It is Php 132,801,000, or 41.99% lower compared to the fiscal year 2026 budget.

4708
04:52:17,620 --> 04:52:21,980
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, this budget is not merely an operational expense.

4709
04:52:22,720 --> 04:52:23,880
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: It is an investment in building more resilient

4710
04:52:23,900 --> 04:52:50,660
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: communities, advancing climate-responsive planning, safeguarding infrastructure and livelihoods, and ultimately securing the lives, well-being and sustainable future of every Filipino. I therefore respectfully seek the support of this august chamber for the approval of the fiscal year 2027 budget of the Climate Change Commission. This representation is now ready for interpellation. Thank you.

4711
04:52:50,660 --> 04:52:52,740
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you, Majority Leader.

4712
04:52:53,900 --> 04:53:03,440
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Iris Marie de Mesa Montes from 4K Partylist.

4713
04:53:03,720 --> 04:53:10,300
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentlelady from 4K Partylist, Representative Iris Marie de Mesa Montes, ma'am, you are recognized.

4714
04:53:10,800 --> 04:53:19,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Distinguished sponsor to the Climate Change Commission, pagandang umaga po.

4715
04:53:19,060 --> 04:53:23,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ilang katanungan lamang po mula sa kababaihan kabalikatan para sa kapakanan.

4716
04:53:23,900 --> 04:53:31,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: At kaularan ng bayan, nabanggit niyo po sa inyong opening statement, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

4717
04:53:32,160 --> 04:53:41,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: na the Climate Change Commission was created to lead, coordinate, monitor, and evaluate climate change programs across government.

4718
04:53:41,960 --> 04:53:49,080
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: This is a very powerful mandate, but the question is whether it is being exercised with enough authority.

4719
04:53:49,080 --> 04:53:53,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: For fiscal year 2027, which agencies, programs,

4720
04:53:53,900 --> 04:54:01,300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: and climate tag expenditures will be the subject to actual review and monitoring by the Commission.

4721
04:54:44,260 --> 04:54:51,460
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, as of this moment, we have 202 NGAs, 98 GOCCs, and 119 SUCs.

4722
04:54:52,420 --> 04:54:53,740
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

4723
04:54:53,900 --> 04:54:55,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

4724
04:54:56,240 --> 04:55:10,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: For instance, if an agency labels a program climate tagged, but it cannot show a clear climate rational or measurable target or credible risk basis,

4725
04:55:11,360 --> 04:55:13,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ano po ang ginagawa ng komisyon?

4726
04:55:14,080 --> 04:55:23,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Meron po bang otoridad ng komisyon na i-question or mag-recommend ng revision or i-flag yung mga items na iyon sa Department?

4727
04:55:23,880 --> 04:55:27,700
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Department of Budget and Management or Kongreso po.

4728
04:55:41,260 --> 04:55:47,140
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, yan ay part ng Quality Assurance ng Climate Change Commission,

4729
04:55:47,540 --> 04:55:52,660
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: and meron silang mga reviews, and then if makapasa, ay okay na sila, Mr. Speaker.

4730
04:55:52,660 --> 04:56:08,480
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, ilan po yung na-review exactly? May datos po ba tayo kung ilang mga climate tag programs ang na-review na ng komisyon na-reject or na-correct in recent budget cycle?

4731
04:56:22,660 --> 04:56:44,980
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, as of the moment, total na NGAs ay 202, ang completed ng process ay 148, with a compliance rate of 73.27%.

4732
04:56:44,980 --> 04:56:51,980
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: For GOCC, 98 ang total completed CCET process, 57, with a compliance rate of 58.27%.

4733
04:56:52,660 --> 04:57:07,700
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: With the SUCs, 119. Completed CCET process, 102. Compliance rate of 85.71%, with a total of compliance rate ng 73.27%, Mr. Speaker.

4734
04:57:08,180 --> 04:57:10,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

4735
04:57:10,940 --> 04:57:19,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, alam naman po natin, isa sa mga problema, actually po pala dalawa, um, dalawa sa pinakamalaking problema natin dito.

4736
04:57:19,280 --> 04:57:22,280
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, isa na dun po yung institutional order.

4737
04:57:22,660 --> 04:57:24,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Overlap. Ano po?

4738
04:57:24,680 --> 04:57:45,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, paano po kino-coordinate ng komisyon at na-avoid yung institutional overlap ng functions, especially with like DENR, um, with the NDRRM, with the DOF and other agencies na involved din sa climate policy, no?

4739
04:57:45,760 --> 04:57:47,920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, disaster risk reduction.

4740
04:57:47,920 --> 04:57:52,640
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, ano po ba talaga, anong role ng komisyon?

4741
04:57:52,660 --> 04:58:02,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Sa coordination, what evidence shows that coordination is producing unified action rather than yung fragmentation pong na meron tayo?

4742
04:58:02,940 --> 04:58:09,500
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, meron namang interagency meetings with the different agencies together with the Commission, Climate Change Commission.

4743
04:58:10,000 --> 04:58:13,340
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: So, walang overlapping of duties and responsibilities, Mr. Speaker.

4744
04:58:14,000 --> 04:58:17,000
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay, thank you, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

4745
04:58:17,000 --> 04:58:22,500
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, pagdating po sa climate finance, this remains as actually...

4746
04:58:22,660 --> 04:58:24,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ...one of the problems, no?

4747
04:58:24,880 --> 04:58:40,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, sinasabi po nila, um, the absence of a climate finance unit is very challenging, kaya nagkakaroon po tayo ng fragmented, minsan underutilized and difficult to access, particularly for LGUs.

4748
04:58:40,660 --> 04:58:51,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, wala po kasi tayong centralized institutional mechanism for climate finance, kaya nalilimit yung abilidad ng ating bansa to effectively mobilize...

4749
04:58:52,660 --> 04:58:57,560
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ...coordinate and deploy both domestic and international resources.

4750
04:58:58,480 --> 04:59:09,540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, while the CCC is mandated to coordinate climate policy, it lacks a dedicated operational arm focused exclusively on climate finance.

4751
04:59:10,000 --> 04:59:16,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po ang posisyon ng CCC on the creation of a climate finance unit under the CCC?

4752
04:59:16,760 --> 04:59:22,640
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, meron na silang development partners coordinating group para ma-discipline.

4753
04:59:22,660 --> 04:59:33,300
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Pag-discuss nila doon kung ano yung mga kailangan gawin para sa Climate Change Commission para, once again, ma-disseminate yung mga information at anong mga kailangan gawin, especially with the LGUs.

4754
04:59:34,040 --> 04:59:43,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Um, yung pinupunto ko po dito, Mr. Speaker, um, Mr. Sponsor, kasi yung iba po, diba, parang dire-diretsyo, iba-diretsyo na sa LGU.

4755
04:59:43,880 --> 04:59:50,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: May fragmentation talaga, halimbawa may financing, diretsyo sa LGU, yung iba-diretsyo dito.

4756
04:59:50,520 --> 04:59:51,880
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Wala talaga siyang centralized...

4757
04:59:52,660 --> 04:59:59,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: ...centralized agency who monitors the financing that comes in para magkaroon ng isang comprehensive...

4758
05:00:00,000 --> 05:00:08,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: or integrated na pagtingin doon sa mga programa o sa mga proyekto na dapat na paprioritize for financing.

4759
05:00:09,180 --> 05:00:13,780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How does the Climate Change Commission deal with that problem?

4760
05:00:15,460 --> 05:00:22,540
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: As I mentioned earlier, Mr. Speaker, because of the interagency meeting, doon nila nabibigay yung mga gusto nila,

4761
05:00:22,960 --> 05:00:27,860
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: ano mga kailangan na kukuha nila para once again walang overlapping with the different agencies

4762
05:00:27,860 --> 05:00:32,660
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: and iba-iba naman yung mga mandates nila with the different agencies, Mr. Speaker.

4763
05:00:34,000 --> 05:00:39,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: How about po, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor, yung pag-access ng mga international grants?

4764
05:00:40,400 --> 05:00:48,720
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po ba ang mga challenges or mga balakid sometimes that we are not able to access grants from abroad?

4765
05:00:49,420 --> 05:00:53,560
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: That remains to be one of the biggest challenges of the Commission, Mr. Speaker.

4766
05:00:54,020 --> 05:00:57,820
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: That is why our Secretary-Holmes,

4767
05:00:57,860 --> 05:01:04,420
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: is also working hard with the different agencies to be able to access some of the finances, international finances, Mr. Speaker.

4768
05:01:04,420 --> 05:01:12,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi po kaya yung fragmentation na ito is also a contributing factor and our difficulty to access international financing

4769
05:01:12,600 --> 05:01:16,120
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kasi po, di ba, hindi coordinated, hindi integrated.

4770
05:01:16,720 --> 05:01:25,540
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So medyo mas matagal, mas minsan, baka po, nagkakaroon ng pagkakataon na deadline na hindi natin na ibibigay ng dokumento,

4771
05:01:25,900 --> 05:01:27,420
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: medyo madaming dokumentong kailangan.

4772
05:01:27,860 --> 05:01:33,460
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Hindi po ba ito isa sa mga dahilan din kung bakit nagkakaroon tayo ng problema doon?

4773
05:01:36,220 --> 05:01:43,260
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Isa po yan sa mga dahilan, Mr. Speaker, pero the Commission is now working on the capacity building para sa NGAs

4774
05:01:43,260 --> 05:01:48,360
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: para ma-improvise, ma-coordinate ang mga different mga agencies, Mr. Speaker.

4775
05:01:51,940 --> 05:01:54,620
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: And under the Government Optimization Law,

4776
05:01:57,860 --> 05:02:04,660
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: yung Climate Finance Unit requested to be established, is requested to be established, Mr. Speaker.

4777
05:02:05,980 --> 05:02:14,440
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: That was my question a while ago, the climate, I asked about your position on creating a Climate Finance Unit.

4778
05:02:14,680 --> 05:02:22,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So, in fact, I think the answer was you have, there's already a coordinating committee.

4779
05:02:23,220 --> 05:02:26,680
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ito pong sinasabing nyo ngayon, ano po yung Climate Finance Unit?

4780
05:02:26,820 --> 05:02:27,340
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So there is...

4781
05:02:27,860 --> 05:02:31,300
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: An existing Climate Finance Unit in the Commission right now?

4782
05:02:31,680 --> 05:02:33,580
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: It is still a proposal, Mr. Speaker.

4783
05:02:33,960 --> 05:02:35,160
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay. Thank you.

4784
05:02:35,820 --> 05:02:41,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So the Commission is supporting the creation of that unit?

4785
05:02:41,540 --> 05:02:42,300
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

4786
05:02:42,300 --> 05:02:49,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: I was leading to that question a while ago, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

4787
05:02:50,000 --> 05:02:56,880
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, Mr. Speaker. In fact, the Commission is also requesting your support, the support of everybody,

4788
05:02:56,880 --> 05:02:59,820
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: especially in the 20th Congress, Mr. Speaker.

4789
05:02:59,820 --> 05:03:05,180
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor, I'd like to inform the Sponsor and the CCC that, in fact,

4790
05:03:05,520 --> 05:03:12,960
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: this representation filed House Bill 8918, creating the Climate Finance Unit in the CCC.

4791
05:03:14,300 --> 05:03:18,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Okay. Next question ko naman po, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

4792
05:03:18,960 --> 05:03:26,360
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Nasabi nyo rin po kanina, every year, communities are hit by stronger typhoons, deeper floods, longer dry spells, extreme heat,

4793
05:03:26,360 --> 05:03:31,260
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: coastal erosion, crop losses, water insecurity, and displacement.

4794
05:03:31,800 --> 05:03:39,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Against this backdrop po, how can the Commission justify its 2027 proposal as adequate,

4795
05:03:39,380 --> 05:03:45,400
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: considering na, sabi nyo rin po, bumaba po yung proposed budget for 2027?

4796
05:03:45,900 --> 05:03:53,600
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ano po, dito sa funding gap na ito, ano po ang mga maaapektuhan na programa at proyekto ng CCC?

4797
05:03:53,600 --> 05:03:55,780
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Alin ang hindi mapopondohan?

4798
05:03:55,780 --> 05:03:57,220
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Alin ang makukompromiso?

4799
05:03:57,380 --> 05:03:59,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Alin ang mapaaapektuhan po?

4800
05:04:08,120 --> 05:04:14,920
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, ang Commission naman ay nag-request na mas mataas na budget, but they also understand the budget.

4801
05:04:18,860 --> 05:04:25,360
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Ang maapektuhan ng mga programs nila, a capacity building for LGU, mga data,

4802
05:04:25,780 --> 05:04:29,340
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: gathering, at sa iba pang mga programs, Mr. Speaker.

4803
05:04:30,220 --> 05:04:35,900
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Doon sa capacity building po, alam ko isang challenge dyan eh, kaya hindi makapag-access.

4804
05:04:36,320 --> 05:04:42,320
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Halimbawa nga yung mga LGU sa People's Survival Fund, kasi nahihirapan po sila doon sa documentation,

4805
05:04:42,820 --> 05:04:50,060
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: sa sobrang dami po ng dokumentong hinihingi, ultimo po paggawa ng project proposal, hirap sila.

4806
05:04:50,340 --> 05:04:52,920
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: So kasama po ba dyan sa capacity building yan?

4807
05:04:52,920 --> 05:04:54,920
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, kasama, Mr. Speaker.

4808
05:04:55,780 --> 05:04:56,580
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Magsalamat po.

4809
05:04:57,720 --> 05:05:09,380
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: On climate disasters and losses naman po, meron po bang estimate ang Commission yung annual economic and social cost ng climate impact sa Pilipinas?

4810
05:05:09,580 --> 05:05:12,140
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Meron po tayong datos tungkol dyan?

4811
05:05:16,980 --> 05:05:21,220
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The Commission has a data, Mr. Speaker, but please allow me to...

4812
05:05:23,220 --> 05:05:25,760
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: But anyways, anyway, Mr. Speaker.

4813
05:05:25,780 --> 05:05:33,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor, ang gusto ko lamang po ito nung tungkol dyan, in general, yung data pong yan,

4814
05:05:33,680 --> 05:05:40,660
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: kung lagi po nating pinupondohan lamang yung ating recovery,

4815
05:05:41,440 --> 05:05:46,860
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: hindi pa kaya dapat mas pagtuuna natin ng pansin yung prevention before disasters?

4816
05:05:47,040 --> 05:05:50,100
Rep. Iris Marie Demesa Montes: Ganoon naman po ang ginagawa ng Commission, hindi po ba?

4817
05:05:50,100 --> 05:05:54,560
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

4818
05:05:54,660 --> 05:05:55,760
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, meron naman po and we agree.

4819
