Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Its future requirements for resources and infrastructure, of course, has potential climate impacts in its geographical location. Considering that there is a statement confirming that there is no environmental impact

5008
05:17:23,500 --> 05:17:40,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: assessment issued yet, how can the Climate Change Commission ensure that any climate-related appropriations connected to the Pax Silica infrastructure are based on a sufficiently supported assessment of risks, environmental impacts, and adaptation requirements?

5009
05:17:40,420 --> 05:17:52,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Paano po i-ensure ng CCC yung kanilang mandato, exercise, na kung anumang budget ilalaan sa Pax Silica in the future or soon ay,

5010
05:17:53,500 --> 05:17:59,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: naaayon sa pag-aaral ng mga risks, impacts, at kung anumang requirements kailangan?

5011
05:18:01,260 --> 05:18:08,000
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, yan ay mandate ng DENR, but the CCC will just assist, Mr. Speaker.

5012
05:18:08,760 --> 05:18:10,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: How would it assist, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor?

5013
05:18:23,500 --> 05:18:34,880
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The CCC will provide a technical assistance, Mr. Speaker.

5014
05:18:35,340 --> 05:18:50,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Technical assistance to clarify, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, kung paano i-ensure na yung appropriations ay may assessment of risks, environmental impacts, at kung anumang?

5015
05:18:53,500 --> 05:19:03,080
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Ang commission mandato ng CCC, Mr. Speaker, ay sa climate lang, but they will provide a climate lens and a projections, Mr. Speaker.

5016
05:19:04,220 --> 05:19:09,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes, that is precisely the point being made by this representation, Mr. Speaker.

5017
05:19:09,820 --> 05:19:22,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May bird's eye view ang CCC kung paano ang certain appropriations dapat pong direksyonan para po naaayon sa targets natin to reduce climate change.

5018
05:19:23,500 --> 05:19:25,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Address it, etc., mitigate it.

5019
05:19:26,660 --> 05:19:34,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May early projections now ang ilang environmental groups that Pax Silica may be detrimental to the environment.

5020
05:19:34,940 --> 05:19:47,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And so, up until now, may mga tumututol sa Pax Silica, pero this administration is adamant on ensuring that it is signed in November.

5021
05:19:48,020 --> 05:19:52,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, ano po bang kayang gawin ng Climate Change Commission na kung anumang budget ilalaan dito?

5022
05:19:53,500 --> 05:20:10,280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And beyond technical assistance on budget tagging sa DNR, ay naayon siya sa climate change mitigation targets, etc. na gusto natin gawin naman ng buong pamahalaan.

5023
05:20:11,060 --> 05:20:20,800
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, ang Climate Change Commission ay mag-assess para sa Pax Silica impacts on climate vulnerability sa NDC and low carbon development. Mr. Speaker.

5024
05:20:20,800 --> 05:20:23,340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May assessment na pong ginawa ang CCC?

5025
05:20:23,500 --> 05:20:24,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor?

5026
05:20:26,880 --> 05:20:29,440
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Sa preliminary pa sila, Mr. Speaker.

5027
05:20:29,960 --> 05:20:36,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, may we receive a copy of this preliminary assessment by the CCC on Pax Silica?

5028
05:20:36,920 --> 05:20:38,960
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, the commission will submit, Mr. Speaker.

5029
05:20:38,960 --> 05:20:41,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you very much, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

5030
05:20:41,980 --> 05:20:53,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang huling tanong nga lang po talaga natin ay dahil po, as per the involvement of climate change expenditure tagging, in line with the current budget appropriated for CCC,

5031
05:20:53,500 --> 05:21:02,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: there is almost a 53% difference, specifically, from P316 million to P183 million pesos.

5032
05:21:02,240 --> 05:21:08,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: With this decrease in the budget, how can we ensure that risk assessment would be strictly implemented?

5033
05:21:09,460 --> 05:21:11,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Gaya po nang sa kaso ng Pax Silica.

5034
05:21:11,600 --> 05:21:18,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And paano ba natin magagaranti na effective po ito with regards with its decreased budget, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor?

5035
05:21:19,340 --> 05:21:23,240
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: The commission would like a higher budget, but because of the budget concerns,

5036
05:21:23,500 --> 05:21:26,900
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: constraints, kailangan lang nila mag-work kung anong nandyan sa kanila,

5037
05:21:27,380 --> 05:21:33,520
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: pero they assure na lahat ng mga kailangan gawin ay magawa ng commission, Mr. Speaker.

5038
05:21:33,640 --> 05:21:38,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Meron po bang functions na siguro mas mahihirapan silang magawa dahil sa decreased budget?

5039
05:21:41,260 --> 05:21:44,960
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: More on the capacity building on the different LGUs, Mr. Speaker.

5040
05:21:45,600 --> 05:21:52,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Which is very necessary dahil separate pa po sa national budget, may budget din pong ginagawa,

5041
05:21:53,500 --> 05:21:54,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: separate din ang LGUs.

5042
05:21:54,700 --> 05:22:01,460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At kung hindi po nila alam kung paano budgetan ng naayon sa National Climate Action Plan

5043
05:22:01,460 --> 05:22:06,800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at paano din pong magtag, mas mahihirapan tayong rumespunde sa climate change.

5044
05:22:07,080 --> 05:22:14,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, this representation joins the different colleagues that have manifested here today

5045
05:22:14,860 --> 05:22:20,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na dapat sana mas kaya ng Climate Change Commission yung kanyang gawain.

5046
05:22:20,440 --> 05:22:23,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At kung ang increase ng budget ang sana,

5047
05:22:23,500 --> 05:22:28,200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung saan ang makakapagbigay nito, this representation will move for that at the proper time.

5048
05:22:28,440 --> 05:22:32,460
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For now, I have no other further questions other than we hope that the report can be submitted

5049
05:22:32,460 --> 05:22:37,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung sana po sa Monday, kung maaari, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

5050
05:22:38,580 --> 05:22:41,500
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Yes, the commission will submit on Monday, Mr. Speaker.

5051
05:22:41,860 --> 05:22:43,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

5052
05:22:46,000 --> 05:22:46,760
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: George Leder.

5053
05:22:48,300 --> 05:22:52,500
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Mr. Speaker, next to interpolate the sponsor, I move to recognize representative

5054
05:22:53,500 --> 05:22:58,560
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Jernie Jett Nisay of Pusong Pinoy Partylist.

5055
05:22:58,780 --> 05:22:59,140
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: So move.

5056
05:22:59,460 --> 05:23:02,420
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Honorable Jernie Jett Nisay.

5057
05:23:03,020 --> 05:23:07,840
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Mr. Sponsor, isang katanungan na lamang po bago ho natin i-terminate.

5058
05:23:08,320 --> 05:23:11,780
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor, ayon po sa latest pag-asa outlook,

5059
05:23:11,980 --> 05:23:16,100
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: ang El Niño ay maaaring magpatuloy hanggang first half of 2027

5060
05:23:16,100 --> 05:23:23,100
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: at maaaring umabot sa very strong state na maaaring magdulot ng mas matinding init at below normal rainfall

5061
05:23:23,500 --> 05:23:26,020
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: sa ilang bahagi ng ating bansa.

5062
05:23:26,760 --> 05:23:32,280
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Pero nakita rin po natin nitong mga nakaraang buwan na marami pa rin pong magkaroon ng episodes

5063
05:23:32,280 --> 05:23:34,400
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: ng matinding ulan at malalakas na bagyo.

5064
05:23:35,060 --> 05:23:40,220
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Sa ganitong pabago-bagong climate conditions, paano po minomonitor ng CCC

5065
05:23:40,220 --> 05:23:43,680
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: kung ang mga LGU ay handa sa magkaibang climate risk

5066
05:23:43,680 --> 05:23:50,860
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: mula sa water shortage at agricultural losses hanggang sa flooding and storm impacts.

5067
05:23:53,500 --> 05:23:59,300
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: What the Commission has is the LC-CAP of the different LGUs

5068
05:23:59,300 --> 05:24:05,660
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: and the CCC is monitoring kung na-implement na ba ang mga LC-CAPs nila, Mr. Speaker.

5069
05:24:13,560 --> 05:24:19,740
Rep. John Geesnell "Baba" Yap: Mr. Speaker, LC-CAP means Local Climate Change Action Plan, Mr. Speaker.

5070
05:24:21,340 --> 05:24:23,340
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor,

5071
05:24:24,020 --> 05:24:27,880
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: nais ko na lang pong ipahayag ang aking suporta sa Climate Change Commission

5072
05:24:27,880 --> 05:24:33,460
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: at sa mahalagang gampanin nila sa paghanda ng ating bansa sa mga epekto ng climate change.

5073
05:24:34,020 --> 05:24:38,700
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Sa uli, ang climate action ay hindi lamang tungkol sa environmental policies.

5074
05:24:39,300 --> 05:24:49,580
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Direktang nakaka-apekto ito sa pagkain at mga presyo, kabuhayan, kalusugan, tahanan, infrastruktura at siguridad ng ating mga komunidad.

5075
05:24:50,280 --> 05:24:52,840
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Kaya mahalaga ang patuloy na tungkulin ng CCC,

5076
05:24:52,840 --> 05:25:01,000
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: upang matulungan ng ating mga ahensya, LGUs at mga komunidad na maisalin ang climate policies at risk assessments

5077
05:25:01,000 --> 05:25:05,900
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: sa konkretong paghanda at mga programang tumutugon sa mga pangailangan ng mamayan.

5078
05:25:06,500 --> 05:25:11,920
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Patuloy nating suportahan ang mga akbang na magpapalakas sa climate resilience ng ating mga komunidad,

5079
05:25:11,920 --> 05:25:19,000
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: lalo na habang mas magiging hindi inaasahan ang epekto ng matinding init, tagtuyot, malakas na ulan at bagyo.

5080
05:25:19,000 --> 05:25:22,900
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

5081
05:25:23,740 --> 05:25:34,540
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: In behalf of the minority, I move to terminate the sponsorship and debate of the budget deliberation of the proposed budget of the Climate Change Commission.

5082
05:25:35,360 --> 05:25:36,460
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: So moved, Mr. Speaker.

5083
05:25:37,020 --> 05:25:38,420
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: What does the House say?

5084
05:25:39,340 --> 05:25:47,440
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: Mr. Speaker, on the part of the majority, we join the minority in the motion to terminate the interpolations on the proposed budget

5085
05:25:47,440 --> 05:25:49,860
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: of the Climate Change Commission.

5086
05:25:50,280 --> 05:25:50,600
Rep. Eduardo R. Rama Jr.: So moved.

5087
05:25:51,020 --> 05:25:58,480
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: There is a joint motion to terminate the interpolation on the proposed budget of the Climate Change Commission.

5088
05:25:58,480 --> 05:26:01,060
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Is there any objection?

5089
05:26:02,340 --> 05:26:10,340
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Hearing none, the interpolations on the proposed budget of the Climate Change Commission is hereby terminated.

5090
