5134
05:34:22,540 --> 05:34:37,060
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: They are Chairperson-Attorney Marites Barrios-Taran, Commissioner Carmelita Abduman, Commissioner Benjamin Mendilio Jr., and Chief Administrative Officer Salvador Sagadal.

5135
05:34:37,060 --> 05:34:49,940
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: We acknowledge the presence of the heads and officials of the Commission on the Filipino Language, headed by Chairperson-Attorney Marites Barrios-Taran.

5136
05:34:50,900 --> 05:34:52,700
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Welcome to the House of Representatives.

5137
05:34:52,740 --> 05:34:55,780
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: You are the Leader.

5138
05:34:57,320 --> 05:35:12,220
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Vice Chair Ed Christopher Go, Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations, to answer questions on the proposed budget of the Commission on the Filipino Language.

5139
05:35:12,780 --> 05:35:16,660
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Honorable Vice Chair Ed Christopher Go is recognized.

5140
05:35:18,660 --> 05:35:22,660
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: Mr. Speaker, it is my privilege to sponsor the proposed budget of the Commission.

5141
05:35:22,800 --> 05:35:49,740
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: ng Wikang Filipino for fiscal year 2027. The Komisyon sa Wikang Filipino carries the important mandate of preserving and promoting the Filipino language, as well as our other indigenous languages across the archipelago, languages that embody the soul of our people. The Commission's approved budget allocation for fiscal year 2027 is around 120 million, but the Commission has identified an additional 27.5 million

5142
05:35:49,780 --> 05:35:52,120
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: For priority programs which are as follows.

5143
05:35:52,740 --> 05:36:04,660
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: Pagbuo ng otografiya para sa sampung matinding nanganganib na wika, pagtatayo ng limang bantayog wika, and implementation of the Filipino Sign Language Visual Communication Assessment for the Deaf.

5144
05:36:06,620 --> 05:36:14,940
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: Mr. Speaker, the Commission ng Wikang Filipino wishes that its budget allocation will be augmented for the proper implementation of its priority programs.

5145
05:36:15,660 --> 05:36:21,920
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: These programs are important in ensuring that our languages remain alive, accessible, and responsive to the needs of our people.

5146
05:36:21,920 --> 05:36:27,080
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: We are hopeful that the Commission's proposed additional funding will be given great consideration.

5147
05:36:27,800 --> 05:36:30,300
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: We are ready to answer questions. Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

5148
05:36:31,160 --> 05:36:31,880
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: Majority Leader.

5149
05:36:32,480 --> 05:36:43,340
Rep. Alyssa Michaela "Mica" M. Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize Representative Renee Louise Co of Kabataan Partylist to interpellate as sponsor on the proposed budget of the Commission on the Filipino Language.

5150
05:36:43,700 --> 05:36:46,840
Deputy Speaker Yasser Alonto Balindong: The Honorable Renee Louise Co is recognized.

5151
05:36:47,540 --> 05:36:49,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

5152
05:36:49,760 --> 05:36:51,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Good afternoon to our sponsor.

5153
05:36:51,920 --> 05:37:00,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And to the Commission ng Wikang Filipino, will the gentleman yield to a couple of questions in relation to the budget of KWF?

5154
05:37:00,640 --> 05:37:00,860
Rep. Ed Christopher S. Go: Yes.

5155
05:37:01,800 --> 05:37:03,200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Good sponsor.

5156
05:37:04,540 --> 05:37:19,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang tatanong natin ay tungkol po sa FSL unit na ginawa sa Commission sa Wikang Filipino, na ang pagbuo nito ay may basihan sa enactment ng Republic Act No. 11106, or the Filipino Sign Language Act.

5157
05:37:19,160 --> 05:37:19,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay.

5158
05:37:19,820 --> 05:37:21,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: By recognizing FSL as the...

5159
05:37:21,920 --> 05:37:28,420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: National and Official Sign Language of the country, it is a groundbreaking law even from an international perspective.

5160
05:37:28,420 --> 05:37:41,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: It is also comprehensive in its scope of six language domains of education, justice, health, workplace, media, and all other public transactions, services, and facilities.

5161
05:37:42,000 --> 05:37:51,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: It is likewise an unusual law, which accepts that the visual, spatial language used by Filipinos is true and legitimate.

5162
05:37:51,120 --> 05:37:51,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And,

5163
05:37:51,920 --> 05:37:53,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: par with spoken languages.

5164
05:37:54,020 --> 05:37:55,980
