5591
06:18:14,300 --> 06:18:21,300
Rep. Gil "KabarangayJr" Acosta: I move to recognize Representative Presley C. De Jesus, Partylist, PHILRECA, for his interpellation.

5592
06:18:22,300 --> 06:18:32,200
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The gentleman from PHILRECA Party-list, Honorable Presley De Jesus. If the sponsor is ready, you may start, sir.

5593
06:18:32,240 --> 06:18:46,500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. And of course, to the good sponsor who is my boss, not only an environmentalist, but also when it comes to energy, he's the master. Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Good morning, Mr. Speaker.

5594
06:18:46,580 --> 06:19:11,120
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Good afternoon. Sorry. Question. Is the good sponsor aware that during the recent haze episode, some parts of the country recorded 24-hour PM2.5 levels of 48 and 46 micrograms per cubic meter on September 1 and 2?

5595
06:19:11,120 --> 06:19:16,180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Some parts recorded PM2.5 air quality index.

5596
06:19:16,580 --> 06:19:23,900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Readings ranging from 203 to 245 up to approximately 211.

5597
06:19:26,740 --> 06:19:44,540
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mr. Speaker, Mr. English Colleague, yung haze na yan, galing yan sa Indonesia. Ang tanging makakatanggal dyan, Mr. Speaker, isang malakas lang na ulan. Iyong ulan na ngayon eh. So ulan na yun. Kalimutan na natin muna yun.

5598
06:19:45,740 --> 06:19:46,260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Diba?

5599
06:19:46,580 --> 06:19:49,700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kung walang ulan, we have to worry.

5600
06:19:50,240 --> 06:19:55,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. I told you. Magdating dyan, magaling talaga si Don Pipito.

5601
06:19:58,460 --> 06:20:02,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Follow up. As a brief context, Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

5602
06:20:03,960 --> 06:20:14,480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: These readings are significant because PM2.5 consists of very fine particles that can penetrate deep into the lungs and enter the bloodstream.

5603
06:20:14,480 --> 06:20:16,480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: With cardiovascular and...

5604
06:20:16,580 --> 06:20:17,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Respiratory effects.

5605
06:20:17,860 --> 06:20:33,740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Again, to clarify those readings, exceeded the 35 micrograms per cubic meter, 24-hour limits cited by Environmental Management Bureau under DAO 2020-14.

5606
06:20:35,640 --> 06:20:37,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But again, you mentioned...

5607
06:20:37,860 --> 06:20:43,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Na ba yun, Mr. Speaker? We are aware of that. 25 micrograms.

5608
06:20:43,860 --> 06:20:46,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh, talagang mabigat yan.

5609
06:20:46,580 --> 06:20:51,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pag it subsists for 24 hours, eh kawawa naman tayo dito sa Manila.

5610
06:20:51,680 --> 06:21:00,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: That's why may warning na tayo na habang nandyan yung haze na yan, but the 25 micrograms, eh, only persisted for a while.

5611
06:21:01,420 --> 06:21:06,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It did not last long. So pagkatapos ng ulan, heavy rain will wipe it out.

5612
06:21:07,000 --> 06:21:13,300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I suppose the rains are welcome in order to answer for your concerns.

5613
06:21:13,300 --> 06:21:16,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I told you, Mr. Speaker, it's good.

5614
06:21:17,480 --> 06:21:20,740
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Follow-up question, Mr. Speaker, this yung sponsor.

5615
06:21:20,940 --> 06:21:25,200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Those readings are classified as very unhealthy. Is it true?

5616
06:21:26,240 --> 06:21:26,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Tama.

5617
06:21:28,160 --> 06:21:30,360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Very unhealthy yan. Tama yan.

5618
06:21:33,260 --> 06:21:44,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And DNR-EMB attributed at least part of this episode to possible transboundary smoke from forests and landfires in Kalimantan, Indonesia.

5619
06:21:46,280 --> 06:21:46,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kalimantan.

5620
06:21:46,580 --> 06:21:49,800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kalimantan is not so much, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague.

5621
06:21:50,300 --> 06:21:53,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang sunog talaga sa Indonesia, nagsisimula yan doon.

5622
06:21:53,180 --> 06:21:59,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kasi hanggang ngayon, nagpuputol pa sila ng second growth para magtanim ng klapasawit, yung palm oil.

5623
06:22:00,300 --> 06:22:04,140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung ang hangin ngayon papunta rin sa atin, eh talagang magsasaper tayo.

5624
06:22:04,380 --> 06:22:06,720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: That's why nga, we are praying always for the rain.

5625
06:22:06,800 --> 06:22:12,040
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: But your sighting of 25 micrograms, mabigat yun.

5626
06:22:12,040 --> 06:22:15,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh, talagang hindi namin pa nandito ang DNR.

5627
06:22:15,120 --> 06:22:16,160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya, Mr. Speaker,

5628
06:22:16,580 --> 06:22:17,360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: distinguished sponsor,

5629
06:22:17,980 --> 06:22:24,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: tagdagan natin, nakita mo yung budget ng DNR, napakaliit para sa pag-safeguard ng ating kapaligiran,

5630
06:22:24,560 --> 06:22:27,080
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: yung ating hangin na hinihinga.

5631
06:22:27,600 --> 06:22:28,960
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh, tulungan mo naman ito.

5632
06:22:30,060 --> 06:22:33,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Imbis na lumaki, noong 2025, 26 lang.

5633
06:22:33,220 --> 06:22:34,840
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: 2026, naging 27.

5634
06:22:35,740 --> 06:22:39,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: At 2024 pala, 2025, naging 26.

5635
06:22:39,900 --> 06:22:43,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ngayon, 2026 tayo, naging 27.

5636
06:22:43,100 --> 06:22:46,460
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sa 2027, 28 lang ang hinihingi.

5637
06:22:46,580 --> 06:22:48,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sos, napakaliit nito.

5638
06:22:48,960 --> 06:22:52,580
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Paano naman yung ating mga kababayan sa buong Pilipinas,

5639
06:22:53,020 --> 06:22:57,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: pag ganyan ang nag-persist yan ng dalawang araw, maraming talagang magkakasakit, Mr. Speaker.

5640
06:22:58,520 --> 06:22:59,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

5641
06:23:00,280 --> 06:23:03,800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And I agree 100% to the distinguished sponsor.

5642
06:23:04,620 --> 06:23:08,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My follow-up question, in fact, EMB Region 12 itself acknowledged

5643
06:23:08,980 --> 06:23:16,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: that at the time, only its Coronadal station could analyze PM 2.5.

5644
06:23:16,320 --> 06:23:23,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Meaning, that similarly elevated pollution in other areas could be difficult to detect or quantify.

5645
06:23:24,400 --> 06:23:26,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this accurate, Mr. Speaker?

5646
06:23:28,440 --> 06:23:33,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Meron silang DNR in order to warn our populace.

5647
06:23:33,920 --> 06:23:35,200
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Meron silang daily advisory.

5648
06:23:36,200 --> 06:23:39,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung talagang ganyan, pag lumabas ka, eh, maglagay ka na ng maskara.

5649
06:23:40,620 --> 06:23:43,360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung hindi mo mapigilan lumabas ng bahay.

5650
06:23:43,360 --> 06:23:46,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pero kung lumabas ka lang, makaosyoso ka lang.

5651
06:23:46,320 --> 06:23:49,180
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Huwag ka na manigarilyo sa labas. Huwag ka na manigarilyo sa labas.

5652
06:23:49,660 --> 06:23:51,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mas grabe yun, Mr. Speaker.

5653
06:23:52,700 --> 06:23:58,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Distinguished colleague, pigilan natin yan na yung advisories ng DNR sundin natin

5654
06:23:58,420 --> 06:24:02,520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: para huwag na lumabas yung pag may ganyan na talagang mataas na yung pollutants.

5655
06:24:02,980 --> 06:24:03,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

5656
06:24:04,020 --> 06:24:06,000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

5657
06:24:07,260 --> 06:24:10,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor, the issue presented here

5658
06:24:10,580 --> 06:24:15,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: is not merely whether DNR can record deteriorating air quality,

5659
06:24:16,320 --> 06:24:21,320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: but whether its monitoring network is sufficiently extensive

5660
06:24:21,320 --> 06:24:26,860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and whether dangerous readings actually trigger timely public warnings,

5661
06:24:27,580 --> 06:24:30,460
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: health coordination, and pollution control measures.

5662
06:24:30,700 --> 06:24:32,980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Would the distinguished sponsor agree with me?

5663
06:24:35,340 --> 06:24:42,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: As of 12 o'clock today, yung Kutabato na talagang doon ang malapit masyado pumunta yung haze.

5664
06:24:42,660 --> 06:24:44,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh, fair na yung...

5665
06:24:44,660 --> 06:24:45,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Fair na yung...

5666
06:24:46,320 --> 06:24:47,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kapaligiran.

5667
06:24:47,840 --> 06:24:50,200
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Medyo makakahinga na sila doon ng tama.

5668
06:24:50,760 --> 06:24:53,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Only in Mindanao area, Mr. Speaker.

5669
06:24:54,320 --> 06:24:54,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mindanao area.

5670
06:24:54,740 --> 06:24:56,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Aba't in Metro Manila, wala na po.

5671
06:24:56,720 --> 06:24:59,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala masyado na ito. The rains will wipe it out.

5672
06:25:00,600 --> 06:25:01,460
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Through rain.

5673
06:25:02,540 --> 06:25:03,900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That's why we need the rain.

5674
06:25:04,480 --> 06:25:04,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you.

5675
06:25:05,580 --> 06:25:05,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Follow up.

5676
06:25:06,020 --> 06:25:11,760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: When these thresholds were breached, what specific DNR protocol was activated?

5677
06:25:11,760 --> 06:25:15,040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can the good sponsor please inform us?

5678
06:25:15,040 --> 06:25:22,540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: To the specific of the protocol, the date it was activated, the public health advisories issued,

5679
06:25:23,200 --> 06:25:26,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: the LGUs formally noticed, whether DOH was formally noticed,

5680
06:25:27,500 --> 06:25:32,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and whether DNR initiated any action under the Asian Transboundary Haze Mechanism.

5681
06:25:33,240 --> 06:25:36,560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ito po ba eh, well coordinated po among our agencies?

5682
06:25:36,560 --> 06:25:40,200
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yes, pinapalaganap natin yung information, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague.

5683
06:25:40,840 --> 06:25:42,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Radio, sa TV,

5684
06:25:43,420 --> 06:25:45,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: continuous naman yung air quality,

5685
06:25:45,040 --> 06:25:47,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: quality monitoring from the 10 in the evening,

5686
06:25:48,600 --> 06:25:50,040
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ayun, naging 2.5 na ngayon.

5687
06:25:51,320 --> 06:25:54,160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Tapos yung mga daily, through daily advisories,

5688
06:25:54,480 --> 06:25:56,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: and radio programs,

5689
06:25:57,400 --> 06:25:59,780
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: na-advise natin yung general public.

5690
06:26:01,040 --> 06:26:05,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

5691
06:26:05,520 --> 06:26:13,160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In connection with this, the NEP sets a 2027 target of 80% of highly urbanized cities

5692
06:26:13,160 --> 06:26:15,020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and major urban centers.

5693
06:26:15,040 --> 06:26:19,280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Within the Ambient Air Quality Guideline Values.

5694
06:26:20,020 --> 06:26:23,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The reported actual in 2025 was 71%.

5695
06:26:23,720 --> 06:26:26,580
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is this correct, Mr. Speaker?

5696
06:26:26,580 --> 06:26:27,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Tama po yan.

5697
06:26:36,500 --> 06:26:43,920
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung monitoring ng DNR, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, ambient lang, meaning to say, outside lang talaga.

5698
06:26:44,160 --> 06:26:44,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay.

5699
06:26:45,040 --> 06:26:48,660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, can you explain what's this 80% compliance means?

5700
06:26:49,240 --> 06:26:51,720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What is the denominator?

5701
06:26:52,520 --> 06:26:59,620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That is, how many highly urbanized cities and major urban centers are covered by this indicator?

5702
06:26:59,620 --> 06:27:04,060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How many cities does 80% actually represent?

5703
06:27:04,820 --> 06:27:09,640
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And which cities failed the standard in the latest complete reporting year?

5704
06:27:23,280 --> 06:27:30,640
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, hindi pa sila nakaka-100% pero information, 70% pa lang.

5705
06:27:31,120 --> 06:27:31,820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 70%?

5706
06:27:32,700 --> 06:27:37,400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Which cities po ang hindi pa failed po?

5707
06:27:38,060 --> 06:27:42,960
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Do you have the cities who failed this test?

5708
06:27:44,020 --> 06:27:44,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Meron pa tayo?

5709
06:27:45,040 --> 06:27:51,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: As far as the monitoring, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleague, yung kanilang mga monitoring aparatos, okay naman yun.

5710
06:27:51,660 --> 06:27:55,080
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya lang, siyempre, they cannot be present everywhere.

5711
06:27:55,740 --> 06:27:57,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: At saka yung haze, we cannot determine.

5712
06:27:58,160 --> 06:28:02,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It depends kung alin ang umiiral na hangin, habagat ba o amihan ba.

5713
06:28:03,080 --> 06:28:04,240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ngayon, habagat pa tayo eh.

5714
06:28:04,340 --> 06:28:06,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Before the end of the month, titira na yung amihan.

5715
06:28:07,180 --> 06:28:07,740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pababa na.

5716
06:28:08,160 --> 06:28:10,740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Doon na naman sa amin, sa Palawan, dadalhin yung haze.

5717
06:28:11,840 --> 06:28:13,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya, mabuti na lang.

5718
06:28:13,560 --> 06:28:16,540
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mabuti na lang, meron kami arplano sa Palawan.

5719
06:28:16,880 --> 06:28:17,960
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Takbo ko agad ako dito.

5720
06:28:18,400 --> 06:28:21,520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya, nandito sa Kongreso, walang masyadong haze dito, Mr. Speaker.

5721
06:28:22,820 --> 06:28:24,880
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

5722
