Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron na po bang application para sa earthballing permit ang 8 puno na ito?

6191
07:05:50,060 --> 07:05:52,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At napag-aralan po ba ng DENR?

6192
07:05:53,380 --> 07:05:54,700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yung tungkol dito.

6193
07:05:54,720 --> 07:06:00,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dito sa ulat na ito, tungkol sa kapalara ng mga puno.

6194
07:06:00,060 --> 07:06:00,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kapalara.

6195
07:06:03,640 --> 07:06:04,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saan ito?

6196
07:06:05,260 --> 07:06:06,040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa Marikina.

6197
07:06:07,400 --> 07:06:08,400
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sa Marikina.

6198
07:06:09,800 --> 07:06:15,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, wala pa po ang application, consultation pa lang.

6199
07:06:16,420 --> 07:06:20,820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: And I will join you to object pag in-earthball yung napakalaking puno.

6200
07:06:21,640 --> 07:06:24,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Dahil ang earthballing ay pwede lang po yun sa medyo...

6201
07:06:24,720 --> 07:06:28,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: breast height, diameter, 45 cm, and below.

6202
07:06:29,320 --> 07:06:32,480
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pwede mo earthball yun, Madam Speaker, the Stringis Kulig.

6203
07:06:32,960 --> 07:06:38,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pero yung akasya na sing tanda ko, e hindi na ma-earthball yun, Madam Speaker.

6204
07:06:38,620 --> 07:06:42,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung 82 years old to 100 years old na akasya, hindi pwede yung earthball, mamamatay.

6205
07:06:43,680 --> 07:06:45,260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mamamatay yun ng mamamatay na.

6206
07:06:45,260 --> 07:06:47,260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung maari, palitan na lang yun.

6207
07:06:47,560 --> 07:06:54,580
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung isang akasya ang putulin na centennial na ang edad, e palitan na lang ng dalawang daang akasya kung saan nila maitanim.

6208
07:06:54,720 --> 07:06:56,720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yan ang magandang...

6209
07:06:56,720 --> 07:07:05,540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Madam Speaker, ang sabi ng ating distinguished sponsor, may consultation pero wala pang application para sa earthballing permit.

6210
07:07:06,200 --> 07:07:13,040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maari bang maibahagi ng ating distinguished sponsor kung ano po ang outputs mula sa consultation na ito?

6211
07:07:13,960 --> 07:07:14,520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Anong output?

6212
07:07:15,580 --> 07:07:16,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Output?

6213
07:07:16,660 --> 07:07:18,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Anong nangyari sa consultation?

6214
07:07:18,280 --> 07:07:18,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Anong nangyari sa consultation?

6215
07:07:24,720 --> 07:07:37,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, from 22 trees, e merong 12 na maybe i-allow nila kasi dati.

6216
07:07:37,400 --> 07:07:38,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung karsada ang gagawin.

6217
07:07:41,540 --> 07:07:44,480
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ah, masi-save pala yung 12 out of the 22.

6218
07:07:45,080 --> 07:07:46,520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague.

6219
07:07:47,440 --> 07:07:47,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes.

6220
07:07:47,940 --> 07:07:50,140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Consultation pala. Wala pang application to cut.

6221
07:07:51,700 --> 07:07:54,140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Madam Speaker, tulad ng nasabi ng ating distinguished sponsor.

6222
07:07:54,720 --> 07:07:59,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Napakahirap po kung i-earthball pa yung mga mature na mga trees.

6223
07:07:59,720 --> 07:08:00,940
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi talaga pwede, Madam Speaker.

6224
07:08:01,460 --> 07:08:07,720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya po, sinusuportahan natin ang panawagan ng mga residente ng Marikina na isalba ang mga puno na ito.

6225
07:08:07,960 --> 07:08:19,100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Bagamat lumiit yung bilang na sinasabi na i-earthball, ay nararapat pa rin na huwag nang aprobahan ng DENR itong earthballing permit

6226
07:08:19,100 --> 07:08:24,700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kung magkakaroon man ng application para sa walong nasabing puno na ito.

6227
07:08:24,720 --> 07:08:31,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ayon sa mga eksperto, Madam Speaker, maaaring umabot ng isang taon ang pag-recovery ng puno matapos mailipat.

6228
07:08:32,320 --> 07:08:42,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ipinapakita rin ng mga pag-aaral na mas mataas ang survival rate ng bata o maliit hanggang katamtaman ng mga puno kapag inililipat.

6229
07:08:42,820 --> 07:08:49,040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mas mahirap din ilipat ang mga malalaki at matatandang puno dahil malalim at malawak ang ugat nito.

6230
07:08:49,040 --> 07:08:54,360
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Tulad nga ng halimbawa na naibahagi ng ating distinguished sponsor.

6231
07:08:54,720 --> 07:09:05,240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron na rin tayong mga karanasan noon, Madam Speaker, sa Baguio City, kung saan mahigit 183s ang planong ilipat para bigang daan ang isang mall project.

6232
07:09:05,620 --> 07:09:16,800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Naaprobahan ito ng DENR, ngunit tuluyan ding naipahinto ng Supreme Court noong parehong taon, bagamat merong ilang puno na naputol bago ang ruling.

6233
07:09:16,800 --> 07:09:22,520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa Cebu naman, nasa 228 trees ang nailipat noong 2023.

6234
07:09:23,320 --> 07:09:24,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Para sa Cebu, Boss.

6235
07:09:24,720 --> 07:09:33,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Rapid Transit Project, gayon man, naiulat na may mga punong hindi nakaligtas sa parehong pagkakataon.

6236
07:09:34,080 --> 07:09:38,920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Doon man sa Baguio, ata meron din po sa Cebu na hindi na nakaligtas.

6237
07:09:39,500 --> 07:09:47,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nananawagan tayo, Madam Speaker, na hindi dapat maging kapalit ang mga proyektong pang-infrastruktura, ang pagkasira ng kalikasan.

6238
07:09:47,980 --> 07:09:54,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sinusuportahan natin ang mga proyekto na pangkaunlaran, ngunit hindi dapat maisakripisyon.

6239
07:09:54,720 --> 07:10:03,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: May mga pagtutol din ang mga residente ng Provident Villages hinggil sa ADB Metro Manila Bridges Project.

6240
07:10:04,020 --> 07:10:13,800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa katunayan, nagsasagawa po sila ngayon ng Stations of the Cross bilang pagtutol sa proyektong magdudulot ng pagputol sa ilang matatandang puno sa Marikina.

6241
07:10:14,260 --> 07:10:20,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa information po ba ng DENR, ito pong consultation ninyo na nabanggit kanina sa Bridge 1 lang.

6242
07:10:20,560 --> 07:10:23,020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron din po bang consultation na ginawa?

6243
07:10:23,360 --> 07:10:24,040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nakaugnay?

6244
07:10:24,040 --> 07:10:28,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nakaugnay ng Bridge 2 and 3, nakaugnay ng Metro Manila Bridges Project.

6245
07:10:29,680 --> 07:10:30,160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saan yun?

6246
07:10:36,840 --> 07:10:47,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Oo. Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, we are with you in preserving all these malalaking puno.

6247
07:10:47,500 --> 07:10:53,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: But if the national project like widening of roads will redound to the communities,

6248
07:10:54,040 --> 07:11:04,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: at saka yun namang malaking puno ay matandang-matanda na, remember, no tree in this planet will survive forever.

6249
07:11:05,280 --> 07:11:10,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Mamamatay din yung punong yan. Tulad natin tao, mamamatay din.

6250
07:11:11,280 --> 07:11:22,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya, yung DENR naman, kung mas tinitingnan nila na mag-benefit doon yung community sa pagwiding ng road,

6251
07:11:22,600 --> 07:11:24,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: kaysa i-preserve ang isang akasya,

6252
07:11:24,240 --> 07:11:26,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: eh magtanim na lang tayo ng dalawang daang akasya

6253
07:11:27,180 --> 07:11:44,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: somewhere else para naman yung paligiran at kalikasan may balik mo yung oxygen at saka pag-withdraw ng halaman ng carbon dioxide from the atmosphere at magbuga sila ng oxygen.

6254
07:11:44,920 --> 07:11:47,640
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: So kung isang puno lang yun at palitan mo ng isang daan,

6255
07:11:47,640 --> 07:11:52,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: kung ang kapakanan ay yung carbon dioxide,

6256
07:11:53,160 --> 07:11:53,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ah,

6257
07:11:53,320 --> 07:11:53,920
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: na kinakain

6258
07:11:54,040 --> 07:11:56,120
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ng halaman at ine-exhale niya oxygen,

6259
07:11:56,580 --> 07:11:59,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ay mas marami ang benepisyo sa maraming puno.

6260
07:12:00,280 --> 07:12:02,180
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: May Madam Speaker, Distinguished Kuling.

6261
07:12:03,320 --> 07:12:05,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang sulirin natin dito, Madam Speaker,

6262
07:12:05,560 --> 07:12:07,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: hindi lang isang punong ating pinag-uusapan.

6263
07:12:08,140 --> 07:12:10,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: May pag-aaral ang Lichelle Technologies

6264
07:12:10,340 --> 07:12:14,440
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na naisumite ng DPWH at ng ADB

6265
07:12:14,440 --> 07:12:19,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na tinatayang nasa 1,069

6266
07:12:19,340 --> 07:12:21,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na trees ang kinakailang putulin

6267
07:12:21,600 --> 07:12:24,360
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa Bridges 1, 2, and 3

6268
07:12:24,360 --> 07:12:27,820
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na kaugnay ng ADB Metro Manila Bridges Project.

6269
07:12:28,220 --> 07:12:30,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa Bridge 1, may 514.

6270
07:12:30,980 --> 07:12:34,020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang update nga po dito, dahil very vocal din yung mga residente

6271
07:12:34,020 --> 07:12:36,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: tungkol sa pagligtas ng mga puno,

6272
07:12:36,760 --> 07:12:39,740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: nasa 20 na lang, 12 maisasalba

6273
07:12:39,740 --> 07:12:44,020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at may 8 na lang na i-apply for earthballing.

6274
07:12:44,660 --> 07:12:47,300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: For Bridge 2 naman, nasa 232.

6275
07:12:47,760 --> 07:12:49,140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Para naman sa Bridge 3,

6276
07:12:49,340 --> 07:12:50,480
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ay 350.

6277
07:12:51,360 --> 07:12:54,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nakita na po ba ng DENR ang pag-aaral na ito?

6278
07:13:04,360 --> 07:13:07,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung Phase 1 daw at saka Phase 2 at saka Phase 3,

6279
07:13:07,940 --> 07:13:08,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: hindi kasama yung Phase 3.

6280
07:13:10,320 --> 07:13:12,580
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sabi niya sa'yo, ano yung, sorry, club speaker.

6281
07:13:12,760 --> 07:13:14,300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ibig sabihin lahat, no?

6282
07:13:14,660 --> 07:13:15,780
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Lahat, meron na.

6283
07:13:16,560 --> 07:13:19,120
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi. Phase 1 at saka Phase 2.

6284
07:13:19,340 --> 07:13:20,780
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Puro pa yung consultation.

6285
07:13:21,040 --> 07:13:22,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Saka wala pa rin application eh.

6286
07:13:22,640 --> 07:13:25,280
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay, walang application para sa lahat.

6287
07:13:25,380 --> 07:13:29,280
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero, itong mga sinasabi na maapektuhang puno,

6288
07:13:29,880 --> 07:13:33,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: lahat po ito ay parte ng tree inventory ng DENR.

6289
07:13:35,920 --> 07:13:40,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Nasa inventory stage pa lang yan sa lahat ng maapektuhang puno,

6290
07:13:40,560 --> 07:13:41,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: madam speaker.

6291
07:13:42,740 --> 07:13:46,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: At saka yung importante, yung community consultation,

6292
07:13:47,020 --> 07:13:49,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: sana nandun ka rin para, madam speaker,

6293
07:13:49,340 --> 07:13:54,740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: para mapagtulungan natin na mabigyan sila ng tamang desisyon

6294
07:13:54,740 --> 07:13:58,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: na kung ang community magsabi, ay putulin na yan dahil matanda na yan,

6295
07:13:58,540 --> 07:14:00,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: palitan na lang natin, ay pumayag na tayo.

6296
07:14:01,280 --> 07:14:03,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pero kung ang community mismo mag-resist,

6297
07:14:03,480 --> 07:14:05,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ayaw nila, gusto nila makitin lang yung karsadang nila,

6298
07:14:06,140 --> 07:14:08,900
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: so be it, madam speaker, distinguished colleague.

6299
07:14:09,180 --> 07:14:13,400
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Diba? Kaysa putulin mo yung 100-year-old, 150-year-old na akasya.

6300
07:14:14,940 --> 07:14:16,680
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, malinaw, madam speaker,

6301
07:14:17,420 --> 07:14:19,220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: wala pang kahit anong application.

6302
07:14:19,340 --> 07:14:24,520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Para sa three cutting permits sa Bridge 2 and 3,

6303
07:14:24,940 --> 07:14:29,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at wala pang kahit anong application sa ngayon na aaprubahan.

6304
07:14:30,100 --> 07:14:30,240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay.

6305
07:14:31,780 --> 07:14:35,760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kung gayon, madam speaker, meron na bang environmental impact assessment

6306
07:14:35,760 --> 07:14:38,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang buong ADB Metro Manila Bridges?

6307
07:14:39,540 --> 07:14:41,460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Paari ba kaming makahingi ng kopya ngayon?

6308
07:14:43,260 --> 07:14:46,740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang magawa nila, per merong yan, madam speaker, distinguished colleague,

6309
07:14:46,740 --> 07:14:48,120
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ay yung AIS.

6310
07:14:48,600 --> 07:14:49,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Magawa lang yan.

6311
07:14:49,340 --> 07:14:50,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pag may application na.

6312
07:14:50,480 --> 07:14:52,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: But, before the application,

6313
07:14:52,320 --> 07:14:53,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: pag meron nang nagre-reklamo,

6314
07:14:53,660 --> 07:14:55,800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: pwede na nila i-eyeball yun, puntahan nila yun,

6315
07:14:56,080 --> 07:14:56,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: i-ocular nila.

6316
07:14:57,260 --> 07:14:59,360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Para lang makita nila kung ano yung gagawin nila.

6317
07:15:00,000 --> 07:15:09,040
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: In the future. So, yung AIS naman, pag meron ng application, bago sila hihingi ng environmental impact study.

6318
07:15:11,320 --> 07:15:17,160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero Madam Speaker, kung sa ECC naman, no lahat ito meron ng ECC, ang Bridges 1, 2, and 3.

6319
07:15:17,580 --> 07:15:22,100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At maghihingi po ng kopya ang representasyon na ito mula sa Gabriela Women's Park.

6320
07:15:22,860 --> 07:15:24,340
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: May ECC ba yung pagbutol ng puno?

6321
07:15:24,340 --> 07:15:38,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: O, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, hindi ko pa alam na meron palang ECC yung pagbutol ng puno.

6322
07:15:38,880 --> 07:15:45,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kasi yung environmental impact study, it will suffice.

6323
07:15:45,720 --> 07:15:52,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Because the AIS will tell you whether an ECC is applicable or not.

6324
07:15:53,200 --> 07:15:54,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: So, ganun yun.

6325
07:15:54,340 --> 07:15:56,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague.

6326
07:15:57,860 --> 07:16:03,360
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon, Madam Speaker, kasi ho, kasabi din sa atin ng DPWH nung hinarap natin ang issue na ito.

6327
07:16:03,480 --> 07:16:04,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kasi sila yung mag-a-apply.

6328
07:16:05,240 --> 07:16:06,240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: DPWH, Madam Speaker?

6329
07:16:06,420 --> 07:16:08,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes. O, sila kasi yung mag-a-apply.

6330
07:16:08,500 --> 07:16:09,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, sinabi naman nila.

6331
07:16:09,580 --> 07:16:11,960
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang proponent, DPWH, Madam Speaker?

6332
07:16:13,060 --> 07:16:23,800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At sinabi nila sa atin na baka yung Bridges 2 ay magkaroon ng pagbabago sa kanilang design.

6333
07:16:23,800 --> 07:16:25,480
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: O kung saan dadaan ang mga lugar.

6334
07:16:25,480 --> 07:16:28,200
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kasi meron din mga pagtutol yung mga villages.

6335
07:16:28,760 --> 07:16:38,940
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang sabi nila, nag-uusap na daw ang DPWH at ang DepDev na magkakaroon ng restructuring sa buong proyekto.

6336
07:16:39,760 --> 07:16:43,860
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang DNR po ba nabalitaan tungkol dito o wala pa sa ngayon?

6337
07:16:45,000 --> 07:16:46,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala. Wala pa, Madam Speaker.

6338
07:16:48,040 --> 07:16:49,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay, Madam Speaker.

6339
07:16:49,380 --> 07:16:53,720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang ngayon naman po sa ibang issue na may kinalaman.

6340
07:16:53,800 --> 07:16:54,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa LLDA.

6341
07:16:55,100 --> 07:17:03,000
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang aming opisina ay nakatanggap ng liham mula sa nagkakaisang mamamayan ng Tadlac 1A.

6342
07:17:04,400 --> 07:17:15,500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ito po ay naka-address sa Department of Environment and Natural Resources, sa DNR, at sa Laguna Lake Development Authority, sa LLDA.

6343
07:17:16,760 --> 07:17:23,500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang sabi po dito, sila daw po ay humihingi sa inyo ng sertifikasyon, ng klasifikasyon,

6344
07:17:23,800 --> 07:17:27,940
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ng lupa para sa kanilang lupa na tinitirhan.

6345
07:17:28,440 --> 07:17:41,540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil sa ngayon po sa kanila, ito daw po ay itinuturing na domain land at bahagi ng hindi maipagbibiling pampublikong lupa, inalienable public land.

6346
07:17:41,940 --> 07:17:47,900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngunit sa ngayon po, meron daw pong nagkiklaim na private owner dun sa kanilang lupa.

6347
07:17:48,540 --> 07:17:53,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Natanggap na po ba ito ng LLDA at ng DNR?

6348
07:17:53,800 --> 07:17:56,800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Naipadala daw po ito ngayong May 2026.

6349
07:17:58,780 --> 07:18:26,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, tungkol doon sa mga nare-reclaim sa Laguna Lake, alam mo naman, na-diyaryo 'yan lately. May mga concerned high individuals na sangkot diyan. Mahirap na magkomento, ngunit ang DENR mismo nagsasabi ay wala pa silang na-issue na reclamation permit. Wala, walang mga na-issue. Ilegal po 'yun, Madam Speaker.

6350
07:18:26,700 --> 07:18:34,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang isyo na ito, Madam Speaker, ay meron ng mga pinapalayas na mga magsasaka at naninirahan dun sa lugar.

6351
07:18:35,680 --> 07:18:44,140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang kwento po nila, noong 1980s, sumubok daw po sila, in early 2000s, na magkaroon ng titulo yung mga lupa na yun.

6352
07:18:44,280 --> 07:18:46,800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngunit ang paliwanag nga sa kanila ay hindi yun pwede matitulohan.

6353
07:18:47,880 --> 07:18:53,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya po, nabigla po sila ngayon na merong private claimant.

6354
07:18:53,960 --> 07:19:00,440
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Na hindi po nila kakilala at niminsan ay hindi nila nakita dun sa lugar na nagsasabi na sa kanila daw po yung lupa.

6355
07:19:00,680 --> 07:19:08,020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon, Madam Speaker, ang punto ng liham na ito na is po nilang mag-ocular visit.

6356
07:19:08,020 --> 07:19:19,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mag-karoon ng inspeksyon dun sa lugar, ang DNR, ang LLDA, para makita talaga nila yung sitwasyon ng pagpapalayas sa mga magsasaka.

6357
07:19:19,740 --> 07:19:23,700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At matiyak natin na mapapangalagaan, hindi lang yung kabuhayan.

6358
07:19:23,800 --> 07:19:34,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Itong mga magsasaka, kundi matiyak din yung kanilang karapatan sa panirahan sa lupa na kanilang sinasaka o malapit sa kanilang sinasaka.

6359
07:19:35,060 --> 07:19:47,800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, lalo na kung mga illegal yun na pagtambak doon at saka in-occupy ng ating mga kapatid na maralita, magsasaka ito o mangingisda?

6360
07:19:48,560 --> 07:19:52,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mga magsasaka at meron din pong ilan na nagfifish pond.

6361
07:19:52,620 --> 07:19:53,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Magsasaka sa pil?

6362
07:19:53,800 --> 07:19:53,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes.

6363
07:19:53,960 --> 07:19:56,460
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sa lupa at saka yung mangingisda sa lawa?

6364
07:19:56,860 --> 07:19:57,140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes.

6365
07:19:57,320 --> 07:19:59,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Tapos sila daw ay matagal nang nakatira.

6366
07:20:00,460 --> 07:20:02,580
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Karamihan yan, yung mga illegal tambak dyan.

6367
07:20:02,900 --> 07:20:09,140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala silang, ang DNR wala pa pong pangkalahatang solusyon dyan.

6368
07:20:09,660 --> 07:20:13,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Dahil hindi man yan na legal na reclamation.

6369
07:20:13,480 --> 07:20:23,760
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung reclamation na yan na pinadaan sa PRA, na binigyan ng PRA ng permit para, tandaan mo Madam Speaker,

6370
07:20:23,800 --> 07:20:30,880
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: kung ang reclamation sa lawa o sa dagat ay land for the landless, that is permitted.

6371
07:20:31,380 --> 07:20:39,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya yung mga maku-occupy doon na kasunod sa pagtambak ng may pahintulot ang PRA ay hindi po yun illegal.

6372
07:20:39,920 --> 07:20:41,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, extinguish kulig.

6373
07:20:41,900 --> 07:20:45,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon Madam Speaker, wala po itong kahit anong permit mula sa PRA.

6374
07:20:45,520 --> 07:20:50,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron pong pribado na pumapasok na gustong magtayo ng resort doon sa lugar at sila ay pinapanayos.

6375
07:20:50,560 --> 07:20:53,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, ang kalawakan ng tinutukoy mo.

6376
07:20:53,800 --> 07:20:57,840
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ngunit dyan sa lawa, wala talagang binibigyan ng permit dyan para mag-reclaim.

6377
07:20:58,280 --> 07:21:05,260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Except yung mga karsada na gagawin dyan na pinag-aaralan pa hanggang ngayon Madam Speaker, extinguish kulig.

6378
07:21:05,720 --> 07:21:17,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yan nga ang dahilan Madam Speaker kung bakit hiniingin ang representasyon na ito na bisitahin natin yung lugar dito na binabanggit sa Purok 1A, Barangay Tadlac, Los Baños, Laguna.

6379
07:21:17,580 --> 07:21:18,720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Madam Speaker, kailangan.

6380
07:21:18,720 --> 07:21:23,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At para makita po ninyo mismo yung sitwasyon at makita natin, marinig natin.

6381
07:21:23,800 --> 07:21:25,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Wala doon sa ating mga kababayan mismo.

6382
07:21:26,020 --> 07:21:32,460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ano ba yung issue? Anong kinakailang aksyon? At paano tayo magtutulungan para matugunan ang kanilang issue?

6383
07:21:32,980 --> 07:21:34,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, extinguish kulig.

6384
07:21:34,580 --> 07:21:42,720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I suggest that yung letter mo na yan, iproward mo sa concerned department sa DNR para matugunan ka agad yan.

6385
07:21:43,080 --> 07:21:43,300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yes.

6386
07:21:43,300 --> 07:21:50,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Para alam mo naman ang DNR kung sino yung walang lupa ay binibigyan, hindi yung maraming lupa ang binibigyan.

6387
07:21:51,840 --> 07:21:53,300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sinisiguro ko yan Madam Speaker dahil...

6388
07:21:53,800 --> 07:21:58,080
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Siyempre, the government is there for the side of the landless.

6389
07:21:58,940 --> 07:22:10,800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Madam Speaker, just for the record po, when this was sent to the DNR and the LLDA, this representation was furnished with a copy.

6390
07:22:11,280 --> 07:22:16,520
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: And with due diligence, we forwarded the letter to the concerned agencies.

6391
07:22:17,880 --> 07:22:23,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: And then, dahil po ngayon, pinapaabot na po natin ulit at sana maaksyonan ito agad ng LLDA.

6392
07:22:23,920 --> 07:22:26,160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat Madam Speaker. Maraming salamat.

6393
07:22:26,300 --> 07:22:29,820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, extinguish kulig. Please give me a copy of that letter.

6394
07:22:30,340 --> 07:22:34,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: And I assure you, Madam Speaker, gagawa ng aksyon yung mga taga-DNR.

6395
07:22:35,840 --> 07:22:36,440
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Majority Leader.

6396
07:22:37,080 --> 07:22:45,960
Rep. Mark Anthony G. Santos: Madam Speaker, next to interpolate the sponsor, I move to recognize Representative Rene Louie M. Co. from Kabataan Partylist.

6397
07:22:45,960 --> 07:22:47,040
Rep. Mark Anthony G. Santos: So move, Madam Speaker.

6398
07:22:47,600 --> 07:22:52,320
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Rene Louie M. Co. from Kabataan Partylist is hereby recognized for her interpolation.

6399
07:22:53,140 --> 07:22:53,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you.

6400
07:22:53,800 --> 07:23:00,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker. And good afternoon to our distinguished sponsor and the Department of Environment and Natural Resources.

6401
07:23:01,400 --> 07:23:10,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May the gentleman yield to a couple of questions in relation to the spending of the DNR as planned by fiscal year 2027.

6402
07:23:10,380 --> 07:23:12,940
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Gladly, Madam Speaker. Extinguish kulig. Go ahead, please.

6403
07:23:13,620 --> 07:23:19,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor. My first question would be in relation to Paxilica.

6404
07:23:20,120 --> 07:23:23,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This representation is heartened to receive.

6405
07:23:23,800 --> 07:23:34,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The at least preliminary briefer from the DNR in relation to its findings of Paxilica with the available information.

6406
07:23:34,180 --> 07:23:42,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We'd like to supplement a little further given that we've been asking various agencies what they know of this project.

6407
07:23:43,120 --> 07:23:53,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And of course, what we would like to ensure and to clarify dahil nakadulot po ito talaga ng maraming mga tanong, concerns.

6408
07:23:53,800 --> 07:23:56,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa mga mamayan tungkol sa iba't-ibang issues.

6409
07:23:57,160 --> 07:24:04,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero ang pinaka-na-perview naman po ng DNR dito ay yung usaping kalikasan, usaping tubig, usaping lupa.

6410
07:24:05,420 --> 07:24:17,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: In the last Committee on Appropriations for DTI meeting, Undersecretary Ridolfo stated that investors are expected to provide their own power and water for the proposed Paxilica development in New Clark City.

6411
07:24:17,520 --> 07:24:23,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But contrary to this, the government, through a Malacañang press conference, has publicly assured

6412
07:24:23,800 --> 07:24:53,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that the said development will have sufficient water without compromising the supply of surrounding communities. The National Water Resources Board reportedly stated that available sources within the project area can meet the proposed facilities' requirements and that community water needs will remain the priority. BCDA has separately stated that the proposed surface water harvesting system could initially supply up to 120 million liters per day, compared

6413
07:24:53,800 --> 07:25:05,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: With an estimated Paxilica requirement of approximately 65 to 90 million liters per day, with potential expansion of the system to 300 million liters per day.

6414
07:25:05,060 --> 07:25:12,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So ang pansin po natin, iba-iba yung nire-report sa atin ng iba't-ibang ahensya tungkol sa tubig.

6415
07:25:12,840 --> 07:25:16,920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yung una, sige pahala po yung Paxilica na maghanap ng tubig.

6416
07:25:17,260 --> 07:25:23,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Tapos ngayon, meron na pong mga iba't-ibang sources na tinutukoy at may pag-aaral at pag-iimbestiga na po.

6417
07:25:23,800 --> 07:25:25,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa kung paano ba bibigyan yan.

6418
07:25:26,260 --> 07:25:33,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So may I ask, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, pwede po bang ipaliwanag ng DENR yung contradictions between the two statements

6419
07:25:33,020 --> 07:25:40,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at ikumpirma sa publiko, once and for all, ano po ba ang totoo at established for the sake of public knowledge?

6420
07:25:41,300 --> 07:25:46,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, my favorite topic, Paxilica.

6421
07:25:49,140 --> 07:25:53,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Out of the more than 3,000 hectares na BCDA property,

6422
07:25:53,800 --> 07:26:00,800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: dyan sa Northern Luzon, 960 lang yung original na envision for Paxilica.

6423
07:26:01,760 --> 07:26:12,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung Paxilica, for the information of everyone, this is just an advanced planning kasi kung mawawala yung Taiwan which has four chips maker.

6424
07:26:12,540 --> 07:26:16,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang isa, TSMC, NVIDA, hindi ko lang matandaan yung dalawa.

6425
07:26:17,100 --> 07:26:22,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung ma-overrun ng China ang Taiwan, ay at least may replacement sila na magpakukunan.

6426
07:26:22,280 --> 07:26:26,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Lahat ng ating kabuhayan ngayon ay dependent na po sa chips.

6427
07:26:27,000 --> 07:26:32,560
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung telepono na ginagamit ng ating distinguished colleague, yung telepono ko,

6428
07:26:33,240 --> 07:26:42,640
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: eh kung wala yung mga chips maker na yan, yung mga drones, yung mga AI instruments,

6429
07:26:43,380 --> 07:26:52,260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: halos lahat ng ating future requirements ay magagampanan ng project na yung Paxilica.

6430
07:26:52,280 --> 07:26:59,960
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Now, if you are so concerned about the water resources in the Philippines, napakarami nating tubig.

6431
07:27:00,940 --> 07:27:06,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi lang natin iniipon yung tubig natin at saka ginagamit.

6432
07:27:06,840 --> 07:27:14,780
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung mapunta ka sa bayan ng Korea, Madam Speaker, lahat ng ridges doon sa bundok mayroong impounding dam sa baba.

6433
07:27:15,300 --> 07:27:21,940
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya maski abot sila ng limang buwan hanggang anum na buwan na ilin ninyo, ay hindi po sila naubusan ng tubig.

6434
07:27:22,280 --> 07:27:25,460
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Doon sa atin, sa Central Luzon, napakaraming underground water.

6435
07:27:25,700 --> 07:27:33,780
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: But if I were the government, I will not allow this kind of project to extract water from the underground aquifer, Madam Speaker,

6436
07:27:34,320 --> 07:27:38,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: because the underground aquifer is not an infinite source.

6437
07:27:40,060 --> 07:27:46,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Walang tubig na nanggagaling sa ilalim ng lupa. Lahat yan ay recharged ng rainfall.

6438
07:27:46,940 --> 07:27:52,140
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Papunta po, nag-infiltrate sa ilalim ng lupa. Kaya na-stack up sila doon sa underground aquifer.

6439
07:27:52,280 --> 07:27:57,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung marami naman ang extraction natin, makakaroon niya ng mga land subsidence.

6440
07:27:58,020 --> 07:28:07,520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya dyan sa Northern Luzon, starting from Pampanga up doon sa mga kabundukan sa Sierra Madre, ay maraming tubig dyan.

6441
07:28:08,260 --> 07:28:11,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ngunit, that is reserved for the communities.

6442
07:28:12,080 --> 07:28:16,760
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: If itong Paxilica, if I were the government, they will have to bring their own power.

6443
07:28:16,980 --> 07:28:18,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: They will have to bring their own water.

6444
07:28:18,860 --> 07:28:21,160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung water naman, ayaw kang create water.

6445
07:28:22,280 --> 07:28:23,960
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: You can rely on the water on the underground.

6446
07:28:24,580 --> 07:28:26,800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: You can rely on the surface water.

6447
07:28:27,440 --> 07:28:38,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung sinasabi nilang 100 million liters a day is only 100,000 cubic meters yan, Madam Speaker, distinguished sponsor.

6448
07:28:38,860 --> 07:28:45,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya naman, kung 10 million liters, 100 million liters ang kailangan nila isang araw,

6449
07:28:46,200 --> 07:28:47,820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: i-reduce mo yan to cubic meters.

6450
07:28:47,820 --> 07:28:49,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi masyadong marami yan.

6451
07:28:49,980 --> 07:28:51,880
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: If you measure, Madam Speaker,

6452
07:28:52,280 --> 07:28:53,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: distinguished colleague,

6453
07:28:53,900 --> 07:28:56,780
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: yung outflow ng tubig natin sa Central Luzon,

6454
07:28:57,320 --> 07:28:59,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: sa Lower Luzon, at saka sa Upper Luzon,

6455
07:29:00,020 --> 07:29:00,960
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: papuntang dagat,

6456
07:29:01,240 --> 07:29:05,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: that is only one second output ng tubig papunta sa dagat.

6457
07:29:05,580 --> 07:29:08,240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya huwag tayo matakot na walang tubig sa Pilipinas.

6458
07:29:08,800 --> 07:29:11,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Napakarami natin tubig dito sa Pilipinas.

6459
07:29:11,420 --> 07:29:12,940
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sobra-sobra ang tubig dito.

6460
07:29:13,460 --> 07:29:18,900
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ngunit, pinagsasayang lang natin, tinatapo natin sa dagat, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague.

6461
07:29:18,900 --> 07:29:20,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

6462
07:29:22,280 --> 07:29:26,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pinagsasayang lang natin dito ay mismong mga anecdotes ng mga pinuntahan nating mga komunidad

6463
07:29:26,740 --> 07:29:30,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na malapit sa ini-estimate na tatayo ang Paxilica site.

6464
07:29:31,020 --> 07:29:32,400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kulang daw yung tubig nila.

6465
07:29:32,840 --> 07:29:36,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Hindi po sila makapagsurvive in a day nang hindi nawawala yung tubig.

6466
07:29:36,720 --> 07:29:40,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, assuming if true yung sinabi po ng ating distinguished sponsor na marami,

6467
07:29:41,260 --> 07:29:46,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ngunit hindi rin po maayos yung sistema ng pagkalap nito at even yung distribution,

6468
07:29:46,260 --> 07:29:51,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: no, sana ito ay mag-reflect doon sa magiging assessment ng DENR,

6469
07:29:51,680 --> 07:29:56,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung paano i-recommend, kung paano kunin ng Paxilica yung tubig nila.

6470
07:29:56,560 --> 07:29:59,600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ngunit ang next natanong ko po, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

6471
07:30:00,000 --> 07:30:14,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Considering that the Water Resources Vulnerability and Sustainability Assessment Program ng DNR is being reduced by 26.73% ng budget sa fiscal year 2027 ng NEP,

6472
07:30:14,300 --> 07:30:23,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: how will WRB finance the additional hydrological and climate risk assessments required by a development of this magnitude?

6473
07:30:23,300 --> 07:30:31,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang na-mention nga po ng ating good sponsor is that this is some 900 hectares or 3,000 hectares in vision.

6474
07:30:32,280 --> 07:30:41,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pag susukatin po ng DNR kung paano po gagawa ng paraan na may tubig po ang mga locators at kung ano pong i-establish dito,

6475
07:30:41,560 --> 07:30:44,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kaya po ba ito ng budget ng NWRB?

6476
07:30:45,360 --> 07:30:50,920
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung budget ng DNR ngayon, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, maliit nga para dyan.

6477
07:30:51,680 --> 07:30:53,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh, kung ako yung gabi,

6478
07:30:53,300 --> 07:30:56,840
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: kung ako yung gobyerno, siyempre, eh paghahandaan natin ito.

6479
07:30:57,560 --> 07:31:00,740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung sinabi ko maraming tubig ang buong Pilipinas, totoo po yan.

6480
07:31:01,480 --> 07:31:03,720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sa district ko lang, I have 27 rivers eh.

6481
07:31:04,440 --> 07:31:11,800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: So, dito sa Northern Luzon, I don't know the count of how many rivers is from the Caldera area going to the east,

6482
07:31:12,120 --> 07:31:17,120
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: from the Caldera area sa Isabela going to the west side.

6483
07:31:17,120 --> 07:31:22,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: At dito naman sa Central Plain natin, yung mga tubig na iimbak sa mga dam,

6484
07:31:22,680 --> 07:31:23,120
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: napagsuburan.

6485
07:31:23,300 --> 07:31:26,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sa dam na i-release, that becomes flood doon sa Pampanga.

6486
07:31:27,120 --> 07:31:33,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh lahat, Madam Speaker, that's why I earnestly urge our distinguished colleague

6487
07:31:33,320 --> 07:31:38,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: to recommend the increased budget of the DNR para naman lahat yan matugunan.

6488
07:31:39,160 --> 07:31:41,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala pa namang application yung silika.

6489
07:31:41,360 --> 07:31:45,520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pinag-uusapan pa lang yung investment forum na nangyari dyan sa BGC.

6490
07:31:46,140 --> 07:31:49,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh, pinag-uusapan pa lang yung mga requirements sa Paksilika.

6491
07:31:49,440 --> 07:31:50,640
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: At saka ilang kumpanya.

6492
07:31:51,160 --> 07:31:53,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung mga kababayan natin,

6493
07:31:53,300 --> 07:31:54,520
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: nag-demonstrate doon.

6494
07:31:54,620 --> 07:31:56,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Nandun si Teddy Casino, nakita ko.

6495
07:31:57,260 --> 07:31:58,080
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Dyan sa BGC.

6496
07:31:58,960 --> 07:31:59,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor.

6497
07:31:59,960 --> 07:32:01,400
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Very premature yung Madam Speaker.

6498
07:32:01,720 --> 07:32:04,580
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kasi hindi pa, naku-quantify, ikaw ilan talaga.

6499
07:32:05,000 --> 07:32:06,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Haka-haka lang yun.

6500
07:32:06,180 --> 07:32:08,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang kuryente gamitin, ganito karami.

6501
07:32:08,300 --> 07:32:09,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang tubig, ganito karami.

6502
07:32:09,960 --> 07:32:11,640
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kulang ang tubig para sa mamamayan.

6503
07:32:12,340 --> 07:32:14,540
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh lahat yan, Madam Speaker, masolusyonan man yan.

6504
07:32:14,620 --> 07:32:15,540
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala mang problema yan.

6505
07:32:16,000 --> 07:32:18,840
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Basta, there is political will.

6506
07:32:19,080 --> 07:32:21,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: It can be done, Madam Speaker.

6507
07:32:21,420 --> 07:32:23,100
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: distinguished colleague.

6508
07:32:23,300 --> 07:32:26,040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Kulig.

6509
07:32:26,660 --> 07:32:32,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang sinasabi po ba ay kung kailangan po ng DNR na tignan

6510
07:32:32,100 --> 07:32:38,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung paano yung hydrological climate risk assessments,

6511
07:32:38,460 --> 07:32:40,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kulang yung budget niya sa ngayon?

6512
07:32:41,380 --> 07:32:41,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: As proposed?

6513
07:32:41,840 --> 07:32:46,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, kung patuloy tayo doon sa diskusyon ng Paksilika,

6514
07:32:46,180 --> 07:32:47,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: abutin tayo ng umaga rito.

6515
07:32:47,800 --> 07:32:49,260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Suggestion ko na lang, Madam Speaker,

6516
07:32:49,420 --> 07:32:51,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ilipat natin yung Paksilika sa Palawan.

6517
07:32:51,220 --> 07:32:52,480
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ako ng bahala sa tubig.

6518
07:32:52,780 --> 07:32:53,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ako ng bahala.

6519
07:32:53,300 --> 07:32:54,200
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ilipat natin yung bahala sa kuryente nila.

6520
07:32:55,380 --> 07:32:56,840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Well, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

6521
07:32:57,120 --> 07:33:02,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We're actually requesting more information on the DNR's budget and their capacity.

6522
07:33:02,760 --> 07:33:08,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: That's why we have to predicate our questions doon sa mga mangyayaring

6523
07:33:08,280 --> 07:33:13,300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: meron ng konklusyon na ganito kalaki ang factory na ilalagay,

6524
07:33:14,200 --> 07:33:17,740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ang konsumo ng ilang factory, ganito karaming tubig, ganito karaming kuryente.

6525
07:33:18,300 --> 07:33:20,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: We will require them to put up their own power.

6526
07:33:20,620 --> 07:33:22,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Just like what I did in Palawan.

6527
07:33:23,300 --> 07:33:29,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang 250 milyong daran na leaching plant, yung sumitomo para ma-process yung mga low-grade nickel ores.

6528
07:33:30,000 --> 07:33:31,280
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Sabi ko, magdalagay ng kuryente.

6529
07:33:31,360 --> 07:33:32,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala kaming kuryente.

6530
07:33:32,180 --> 07:33:32,800
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Naglagay sila.

6531
07:33:33,220 --> 07:33:35,080
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: 43 megawatt o coal plant.

6532
07:33:35,460 --> 07:33:36,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala naman nakreklamo.

6533
07:33:36,520 --> 07:33:37,340
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Maraming nakatrabaho.

6534
07:33:37,760 --> 07:33:38,360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Happy lahat.

6535
07:33:38,740 --> 07:33:39,960
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi naupas ang tubig namin.

6536
07:33:40,800 --> 07:33:43,060
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, ganun dapat.

6537
07:33:43,940 --> 07:33:49,620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero, so Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, I'd like to take your answer dahil nga po tinatanong natin,

6538
07:33:49,620 --> 07:33:53,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: may inaasahan tayo at nabigay.

6539
07:33:53,300 --> 07:34:01,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kaya, maliit ang budget, hindi enough at kailangan ng mas marami kung kailangan pong gawin yung impact assessment na ito

6540
07:34:01,180 --> 07:34:07,040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in terms of yung water na iko-konsumo, if ever, ng sapak silika.

6541
07:34:07,320 --> 07:34:09,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But nonetheless, Madam Speaker, ang next naman nating tanong,

6542
07:34:10,420 --> 07:34:14,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: dahil may na-mention na nga po, inaasahang El Nino,

6543
07:34:15,240 --> 07:34:19,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: will that also be part of the agency's assessment?

6544
07:34:19,300 --> 07:34:23,280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung titignan nga po yung mga konsumo na,

6545
07:34:23,300 --> 07:34:26,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na gagamitin ng buong inisiyative na ito,

6546
07:34:26,780 --> 07:34:32,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: anong assumptions po ba ang gagamitin concerning dry season river flows,

6547
07:34:32,760 --> 07:34:34,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: drought and El Nino conditions,

6548
07:34:35,040 --> 07:34:36,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: groundwater recharge,

6549
07:34:36,860 --> 07:34:37,880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: agricultural demand,

6550
07:34:38,240 --> 07:34:39,340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: future population growth,

6551
07:34:39,420 --> 07:34:42,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: will these be part of DNR's assessment?

6552
07:34:43,340 --> 07:34:46,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, yung executive,

6553
07:34:47,620 --> 07:34:49,400
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: we'll cross the bridge when we get there.

6554
07:34:50,000 --> 07:34:50,920
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala pa ngayon yan eh.

6555
07:34:51,040 --> 07:34:52,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Lahat yan ang nakaplano pa lang.

6556
07:34:52,380 --> 07:34:53,020
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: In fact,

6557
07:34:53,300 --> 07:34:56,900
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: wala pang masyadong yung BCDA,

6558
07:34:57,080 --> 07:35:01,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: that's why it was pinpointed because of the ease of securing the land.

6559
07:35:02,220 --> 07:35:05,180
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Meron naman nagsasabi na yung mga katutubo doon, merong claim.

6560
07:35:05,760 --> 07:35:07,500
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh madari, naman yung pacified eh.

6561
07:35:07,620 --> 07:35:10,240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Tabi mo lang sila, bigyan mo sila ng kabuhayan doon sa,

6562
07:35:10,920 --> 07:35:15,460
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: huwag silang mag-claim dyan sa envision as 960 hectares na yan.

6563
07:35:16,080 --> 07:35:19,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: That's more than 3,000 hectares yung BCDA dyan sa Northern Luzon.

6564
07:35:20,520 --> 07:35:22,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: So wala pang in-endorse,

6565
07:35:22,680 --> 07:35:25,340
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: wala pang binigay ang executive dito sa DNR

6566
07:35:25,880 --> 07:35:28,300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: kung ano yung mga parameters na pag-aralan nila.

6567
07:35:28,500 --> 07:35:32,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi pwede na mabasa mo lang sa dyaryo yung DNR, magre-react ka agad.

6568
07:35:32,540 --> 07:35:33,300
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala man sila.

6569
07:35:33,700 --> 07:35:36,840
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kanino nila, Madam Speaker, i-request yung AIA,

6570
07:35:37,060 --> 07:35:39,160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: yung Environmental Impact Study?

6571
07:35:39,200 --> 07:35:40,720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala eh. Wala pa nag-a-apply eh.

6572
07:35:41,240 --> 07:35:44,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Meron nga nagsasabi na sa dyaryo na yan,

6573
07:35:44,920 --> 07:35:48,400
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: kaya nga nung isang araw na nakita ko,

6574
07:35:48,660 --> 07:35:51,180
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: may mga kababayan natin nag-demonstrate doon sa

6575
07:35:51,600 --> 07:35:52,480
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: kung saan na

6576
07:35:52,480 --> 07:35:53,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ginawa yung Investment Forum,

6577
07:35:54,240 --> 07:35:55,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: eh that is too early.

6578
07:35:55,980 --> 07:36:00,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: That is too eager to, too soon to say na masama yung Paxilica.

6579
07:36:00,820 --> 07:36:02,720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero Madam Speaker, good sponsor,

6580
07:36:02,740 --> 07:36:05,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: naghahanda na po ba ang DNR dito?

6581
07:36:05,480 --> 07:36:10,820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I assume kahit po preliminary preparations para po mangyari ito,

6582
07:36:11,160 --> 07:36:15,340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: dapat po ina-undertake na, may earmarking na pong nangyayari

6583
07:36:15,540 --> 07:36:19,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: para po kung ano man po yung output ay handa ang DNR.

6584
07:36:20,780 --> 07:36:22,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pangunguna lang.

6585
07:36:22,480 --> 07:36:25,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: At dahil dyan sa Pampanga River at saka yung Bulacan River, palaging may baha.

6586
07:36:26,240 --> 07:36:29,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung DNR, meron na silang assessment doon sa Pampanga River. Una pa lang yan.

6587
07:36:30,280 --> 07:36:35,360
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pag yung Pampanga River at saka yung Bulacan River, nakapture nila yan at sinannel nila papuntang Paxilica,

6588
07:36:35,540 --> 07:36:38,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: sobra-sobra na yung tubig doon, Madam Speaker, Stingvisco League.

6589
07:36:38,720 --> 07:36:40,820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Malulunod yung mga foreign investor dyan.

6590
07:36:41,360 --> 07:36:45,240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh nagre-reklamo na nga si Congresswoman Bundog sa akin na palaging may baha doon eh.

6591
07:36:45,480 --> 07:36:48,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh kung matsannel lang natin yung baha na yung papunta sa Paxilica,

6592
07:36:49,060 --> 07:36:50,000
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: ang tubig,

6593
07:36:50,440 --> 07:36:51,720
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: maski gaano kadumi,

6594
07:36:51,720 --> 07:36:53,200
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: napakadali ilinisin.

6595
07:36:54,260 --> 07:36:58,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, hihingi na lang po ang representasyon na ito

6596
07:36:58,480 --> 07:37:03,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng kopya ng existing hydrological assessments,

6597
07:37:03,480 --> 07:37:06,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: lalo na po may El Nino din naman din pong parating,

6598
07:37:06,540 --> 07:37:12,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: inaasahan natin maapektahan din po ang Region 3 at mga karating na region, lalo na po ang Tarlac.

6599
07:37:12,640 --> 07:37:16,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lalo na po at gagamitin din po ito sa Paxilica kung ito ay itatayo.

6600
07:37:17,140 --> 07:37:21,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Pag natapos, Madam Speaker, ang assessment nila pampanga river at saka yung Bulacan River,

6601
07:37:21,720 --> 07:37:25,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I'll get a copy for you, ah, these two English colleagues. Walang problema.

6602
07:37:25,900 --> 07:37:26,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

6603
07:37:26,480 --> 07:37:27,180
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: At your service.

6604
07:37:27,760 --> 07:37:28,500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Good sponsor.

6605
07:37:29,240 --> 07:37:36,560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang susunod po nating tanong ay pang-call naman po sa Critical Minerals Agreement na ang tingin nga po natin ay may connection eh.

6606
07:37:36,900 --> 07:37:46,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero nonetheless, ang gusto ko pong itanong, ito po ay isang February 2026 agreement na pinasukan ng Pilipinas at ng Estados Unidos.

6607
07:37:46,560 --> 07:37:50,440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: From the United States State Department fact sheet,

6608
07:37:50,440 --> 07:37:59,740
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: meron daw pong 38 memoranda of understanding or minerals frameworks that they've agreed with other countries.

6609
07:38:00,080 --> 07:38:06,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This is 38. Isa lang yung Pilipinas sa maraming sumama na may ganitong mga endeavors.

6610
07:38:06,680 --> 07:38:19,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At sa pagkakalap at pag-analisa ng mamamayan ng publicly available pronouncements and documents, nakikita na 27 such deals exist.

6611
07:38:20,440 --> 07:38:25,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: To date, this is 15 MOUs and 12 framework agreements.

6612
07:38:25,620 --> 07:38:35,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Less than half of the MOUs announced have been made fully public, only two of which were released by the U.S. government, and the rest are public thanks to partner countries.

6613
07:38:35,960 --> 07:38:47,580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At gusto ko lang pong magbigay ng konteksto na isa rin po ang Myanmar na may single mine na sinuspende ang operations in 2023.

6614
07:38:47,580 --> 07:38:49,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At nung nangyari po iyon,

6615
07:38:50,440 --> 07:39:08,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at meron din naman po na mga ibat-ibang endeavors by which yung pagmimina kapag ito'y nakakompromise by U.S. sanctions, the world supply suffers.

6616
07:39:09,860 --> 07:39:14,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang tanong po natin, nakakuha na po tayo ng kopya ng Memorandum of Understanding

6617
07:39:14,760 --> 07:39:17,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng Critical Minerals na...

6618
07:39:18,360 --> 07:39:19,760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: on Critical Minerals.

6619
07:39:20,440 --> 07:39:21,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng U.S. at Pilipinas.

6620
07:39:22,320 --> 07:39:24,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At DENR po ang signatory dito.

6621
07:39:24,620 --> 07:39:31,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Tinanong po natin yung DFA kung may kopya sila, may wisdom po ba sa pag-enter nito.

6622
07:39:32,960 --> 07:39:40,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang sinasabi po nila, huli DENR yung naglatag ng pangailangan nito at nag-agree nito.

6623
07:39:40,640 --> 07:39:43,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And can I get a preliminary confirmation?

6624
07:39:44,520 --> 07:39:49,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Meron daw pong national importance document na tinransmit ang DENR.

6625
07:39:50,440 --> 07:39:58,240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa DFA, na kaya po ay na mabilis na napirmahan ang Critical Minerals MOU.

6626
07:39:58,380 --> 07:40:00,200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this correct, Madam Speaker? Good sponsor?

6627
07:40:01,960 --> 07:40:06,400
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, synopsis pa lang yun.

6628
07:40:07,700 --> 07:40:13,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Bigyan kita ng kopya nito para at least kung may akahaka, may mga katanungan.

6629
07:40:13,940 --> 07:40:14,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Wala pa yun.

6630
07:40:15,100 --> 07:40:17,740
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh yung EO tungkol sa Critical Minerals.

6631
07:40:17,740 --> 07:40:19,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: If you ask me,

6632
07:40:20,440 --> 07:40:22,640
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: saan ka ba, Madam Speaker?

6633
07:40:23,320 --> 07:40:26,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yung mineral na natutulog doon sa ilalim ng bundok o sa ilalim ng lupa,

6634
07:40:27,760 --> 07:40:30,400
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: eh dapat pakinabangan na yan sa henerasyon na ito.

6635
07:40:30,960 --> 07:40:34,700
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kung hindi man maubos yan, then we will reserve it for the next generation.

6636
07:40:35,700 --> 07:40:39,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh aanhin mo yung mineral na yun kung hindi ma-extract ng tama.

6637
07:40:39,720 --> 07:40:43,340
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Provided, during the extraction process,

6638
07:40:43,340 --> 07:40:49,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: the environmental requirements are fully complied with.

6639
07:40:50,320 --> 07:40:50,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi.

6640
07:40:50,440 --> 07:40:56,820
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi natin sinisira yung kapaligiran kasi hindi naman nangangahulugan na pag hinukay mo yung lupa,

6641
07:40:57,420 --> 07:40:59,260
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: isinira mo na kaagad yung kapaligiran.

6642
07:40:59,840 --> 07:41:03,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Eh pag hinukay mo, kinuha mo yung mineral, tinabakan mo ulit, tinanamay mo ng puno,

6643
07:41:03,520 --> 07:41:04,860
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: sino pa makakita, di wala na.

6644
07:41:05,580 --> 07:41:05,920
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi ba?

6645
07:41:06,540 --> 07:41:14,660
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: So, but the DNR must be the policeman of the whole country in extraction of the minerals.

6646
07:41:14,660 --> 07:41:19,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Ang ibig-ibig, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, na yung DNR natin ay inutil.

6647
07:41:20,020 --> 07:41:20,420
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I don't know.

6648
07:41:20,440 --> 07:41:21,320
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I don't subscribe to that.

6649
07:41:21,700 --> 07:41:22,680
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Hindi naman sila inutil.

6650
07:41:23,140 --> 07:41:24,460
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kulang lang sila sa budget.

6651
07:41:25,000 --> 07:41:32,160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Kaya nga, I request, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, that you move to increase the budget of the DNR

6652
07:41:32,160 --> 07:41:41,160
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: para mas mapangalagaan ang ating kabundukan, kagubatan, at saka sa ilalim ng lupa ito.

6653
07:41:41,400 --> 07:41:44,240
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: I'll give you a copy of this so that hindi nakakahaka.

6654
07:41:44,580 --> 07:41:48,120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I would like to request din as well and we'll wait for that document.

6655
07:41:48,120 --> 07:41:49,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pero, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, ang tanong ko po.

6656
07:41:50,440 --> 07:41:59,660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Tama po ba that the DNR transmitted to the DFA national significance or national importance document or certification

6657
07:41:59,660 --> 07:42:08,320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na yun po ang naging key na mas mabilis na napirmahan at na-finalize in Critical Minerals Memorandum of Understanding.

6658
07:42:08,440 --> 07:42:08,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Is this correct?

6659
07:42:10,640 --> 07:42:14,220
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: On the claim that the MOU was kept secret.

6660
07:42:15,840 --> 07:42:16,980
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Title of the MOU.

6661
07:42:16,980 --> 07:42:19,440
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: MOU, remember, is not an MOA.

6662
07:42:19,780 --> 07:42:20,160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes, po.

6663
07:42:20,160 --> 07:42:22,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: I'd actually ask, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

6664
07:42:22,300 --> 07:42:28,600
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Between the government of the Republic of the Philippines and the government of the United States of America

6665
07:42:28,600 --> 07:42:36,620
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: concerning cooperation to diversify globally critical mineral supply chains and promote investment.

6666
07:42:36,960 --> 07:42:37,840
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Yun lang po, yun eh.

6667
07:42:38,720 --> 07:42:40,640
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: MOU lang, hindi MOA.

6668
07:42:42,180 --> 07:42:45,380
Deputy Speaker Jose C. Alvarez: Memorandum of Understanding has no financial impact.

6669
07:42:46,520 --> 07:42:49,700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May I get a confirmation on the question, Madam Speaker, good sponsor?

6670
07:42:50,160 --> 07:43:00,140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Did the DNR issue a national significance certification that allowed the passage of the Critical Minerals MOU?

6671
07:43:01,940 --> 07:43:04,180
