Rep. Marlyn L. Primicias-Agabas: I move that

8937
09:14:53,680 --> 09:14:55,480
Rep. Marlyn L. Primicias-Agabas: Honorable Sarah Elago

8938
09:14:55,480 --> 09:14:56,600
Rep. Marlyn L. Primicias-Agabas: of Gabriela Party-list

8939
09:14:56,600 --> 09:14:57,540
Rep. Marlyn L. Primicias-Agabas: be recognized to explain her vote.

8940
09:14:58,080 --> 09:15:03,750
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Sarah Jane Elago of Gabriela Women's Party-list is hereby recognized to explain her vote. She has three minutes.

8941
09:15:04,760 --> 09:15:12,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: This representation from Gabriela, Women's Party, votes no to House Bill No. 9642 or the proposed new Espionage Bill.

8942
09:15:13,060 --> 09:15:16,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Malawak ang definisyon ng espionage sa ilalim ng Section 5.

8943
09:15:16,920 --> 09:15:25,100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa panukalang batas, maaaring ituring na espionage ang mga gawaing sinasabing nagdudulot o maaaring magdulot ng pinsala sa Estado.

8944
09:15:25,100 --> 09:15:33,860
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Malabo at malawak ang ganitong pamantayan at nagbubukas ito ng possibility na gamitin laban sa lehitimong kritisismo.

8945
09:15:34,340 --> 09:15:43,920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa ilalim ng seksyong ito, habang buhay na pagkakakulong ng walang benefit of parole at benefits of good conduct time allowance ang parusa.

8946
09:15:43,920 --> 09:15:49,940
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa kasalukuyang kalagayan kung saan ang mga kritiko ng pamahalaan ay nababansagan na terorista,

8947
09:15:50,380 --> 09:15:54,920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: napakamapanganib ng isang panukalang batas na maaaring magturing sa paglalabas.

8948
09:15:55,100 --> 09:16:07,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Paglalantad ng korupsyon, pagbatiko sa mga palisiya o paglalabas ng impormasyong nasa interes ng publiko bilang isang uri ng quote-unquote injury to the state.

8949
09:16:07,380 --> 09:16:21,300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: The bill also expands the definition of critical infrastructure to shield private corporate interest by including telecommunications, energy and food security under the umbrella of espionage protection.

8950
09:16:22,140 --> 09:16:24,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: The bill effectively bans the public from scrutinizing.

8951
09:16:25,100 --> 09:16:27,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: The industries that most affect their lives.

8952
09:16:28,040 --> 09:16:36,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nagbibigay ang panukala ng mas malawak na kapangyarihan para sa surveillance at pagmonitor ng mga communication at financial transactions.

8953
09:16:37,020 --> 09:16:49,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa section 16 at section 17, sa pamamagitan ng pag-bypass sa anti-wiretapping law at pagbibigay ng kapangyarihan sa AMLAC na i-freeze ang mga pondo batay lamang sa hinala,

8954
09:16:49,060 --> 09:16:54,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ginagawa nitong normal ang surveillance, harassment at pag-target sa mga kritiko.

8955
09:16:55,100 --> 09:17:10,780
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maaaring gamitin ang ganitong malawak na kapangyarihan upang matahimik o patahimikin ang mga naglalantad ng katotohanan sa mga katiwalian at umaalma laban sa mga mapanupil at mapang-abuso na palisiya.

8956
09:17:11,140 --> 09:17:16,460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil dito, ang Gabriela Women's Party ay bumuboto ng no sa House Bill No. 9642.

8957
09:17:16,920 --> 09:17:17,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat.

8958
09:17:18,680 --> 09:17:19,300
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Majority Leader.

8959
09:17:19,780 --> 09:17:24,320
Rep. Marlyn L. Primicias-Agabas: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize Honorable Antonio Tinio of ACT Teachers to explain his vote.

8960
09:17:24,760 --> 09:17:29,100
Deputy Speaker Mercedes K. Alvarez: Representative Antonio Tinio of ACT Teachers Party-list is hereby recognized to explain his vote.

8961
09:17:30,180 --> 09:17:31,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker.

8962
09:17:32,360 --> 09:17:38,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: First of all, we note that some effort has been made during the period of amendments,

8963
09:17:39,460 --> 09:17:51,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: effort by the sponsors to introduce certain amendments that would somehow limit the scope of certain provisions.

8964
09:17:53,220 --> 09:17:54,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thereby,

8965
09:17:55,100 --> 09:18:22,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: acknowledging our essential critique that the definitions and the scope and coverage of the bill is so overly broad that it poses threat and danger to the rights and civil liberties of Filipinos.

8966
09:18:23,220 --> 09:18:26,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In the name of national security.

8967
09:18:28,420 --> 09:18:32,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, these amendments have not gone far enough.

8968
09:18:32,500 --> 09:18:47,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, nananatili pa rin po ang masaklaw na coverage ng national security, ng critical infrastructure, ng mga pinagbabawal na acto,

8969
09:18:47,260 --> 09:18:51,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na nanatiling banta.

8970
09:18:53,220 --> 09:19:06,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang panukalang batas na ito, lalo na para sa mga kritiko at mga tumututol at lumalaban para sa kanilang karapatan.

8971
09:19:06,900 --> 09:19:19,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya maaaring gamitin ang panukalang batas na ito bilang isa na namang instrumento, dagdag na instrumento,

8972
09:19:19,200 --> 09:19:34,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: para sa pagsupil ng fundamental rights ng mamamayang Pilipino to free expression, the right to dissent in the name of national security.

8973
09:19:35,420 --> 09:19:39,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Katulad din ng anti-terror law at mga kaugnay na batas.

8974
09:19:39,400 --> 09:19:49,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya dahil po rito ay bumuboto tayo ng no sa panukalang batas, an act expanding the coverage of espionage law.

8975
09:19:49,200 --> 09:19:51,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat Madam Speaker.

